\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korean won rises but suspected  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  caps  \b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2006\par 01:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to midday)  \par \par \uc2 0255 GMT - The South Korean won <KRW=> gains against the dollar, after an unexpected rise in Japan's October industrial output reinforced expectations for a near-term rate hike, sending the yen sharply higher.  \par \par \uc2 - The won also receives support after upbeat South Korean current account surplus data, though its gains are limited as dealers suspect fresh government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 - The won <KRW=> quoted at 929.4/9.9 per dollar, compared to the previous close of 930.5.  \par \par \uc2 - "Offshore investors sold dollars for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Japan's industrial output data came out robust," a foreign bank dealer says. "But the government is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the won sporadically, limiting its gains."  \par \par \uc2 - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  recorded its biggest current account surplus for five months in October from September, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Wednesday, giving an additional boost to the already bullish won. [ID:nSEO184210]  \par \par \uc2 - The country's current account surplus in October rose to a seasonally adjusted $723 million, the biggest since a $1.19 billion surplus in May, from a revised $426 million surplus in September, the Bank of Korea said.  \par \par \uc2 - South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is confident the $4 billion current account surplus target for the whole of this year will be achieved, a senior official at the Bank of Korea says on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 - Japan's industrial output rose unexpectedly in October, underscoring the view that the economy remains on course for steady expansion. [ID:nT145776]  \par \par \uc2 - The yen <JPY=> quoted at 115.66/69 per dollar, compared with around 116.09 in late New York trade.  \par \par \uc2 - Seoul's benchmark stock index <.KS11> up 0.80 percent, with foreign investors selling a net 74.1 billion won worth of shares on the main board.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                     0255 GMT    0015 GMT   prev close\par  Won <KRW=>           929.4/9.9   930.4/1.1        930.5\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>   8.0320/08   8.0283/56       8.0146\par  KOSPI <.KS11>         1,422.83    1,418.52     1,411.47\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061202e2bt0000m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
