\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-S.Korea Oct c/a surplus hits 5-mth high  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Lee Jin-joo and Yoo Choonsik  \par \uc2 527 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 2006\par 00:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  (Updates with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official, won)  \par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Nov 29 (Reuters) - South Korea recorded its biggest current account surplus for five months in October, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Wednesday, underlining the government's difficulty in curbing the won's strength.  \par \par \uc2  However, given expectations that the current account surplus will deteriorate next year, the broad measure of trade flows is unlikely to offer the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  support longer term.  \par \par \uc2  "The trade surplus will probably be sustained next year but the overall current account balance will worsen due to (a) growing deficit in the services account," said Park Yong-il, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at DBS Bank's Seoul branch.  \par \par \uc2  October's current account surplus was a seasonally adjusted $723 million, the biggest since a $1.19 billion surplus in May and swelling from a revised $426 million surplus in September, the Bank of Korea said.  \par \par \uc2  South Korea, Asia's third-biggest economy, has become more dependent on exports for growth this year as domestic demand has cooled.  \par \par \uc2  But at the same time authorities are battling to control the won's strength to keep exports competitive as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has risen to nine-year highs against the dollar and the yen.  \par \par \uc2  The won was up 0.1 percent on the day against the dollar, showing little reaction to the data, partly because of expectations the current account will weaken next year, a trend that is already underway.  \par \par \uc2  The current account surplus for the first 10 months of this year plunged to a seasonally adjusted $1.97 billion from a $14.12 billion surplus a year earlier, the Bank of Korea data showed.  \par \par \uc2  The surplus has been eroded by higher global energy prices and increased spending by Koreans abroad due to the won's strength.  \par \par \uc2  The Organisation for Economic Co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Development said in a report on Tuesday it expected a current account surplus equivalent to 0.3 percent of gross domestic product this year to swing by 2008 to a deficit of 0.4 percent of GDP.  \par \par \uc2  The jump in the current account in October was mostly generated by a rise in the merchandise trade surplus to $2.71 billion from a revised $2.13 billion surplus in September, offsetting a slightly expanded deficit in services.  \par \par \uc2  The won has gained more than 8 percent this year and earlier this month hit its strongest bid level in more than nine years against both the dollar and the yen <JPYKRW=>.  \par \par \uc2  It has since fallen back slightly in what dealers said was heavy government \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  A senior \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  would achieve a $4 billion current account surplus in 2006 "without much difficulty".  \par \par \uc2  However, that would still show a sharp drop from a $16.56 billion surplus in 2005.  \par \par \uc2  Jeong Sam-yong, head of the Bank of Korea's international balance of payments team, said the unadjusted current account surplus in November would be similar to the $1.73 billion surplus recorded for October.     \par \par \uc2 KOREA-ECONOMY/CURRENT (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061128e2bs002fi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
