\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia rallies, central banks watch closely  \b0\par\par\uc2 836 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2006\par 04:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Nov 23 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallied on Thursday, with the Singapore dollar hitting a nine-year high and the Philippine peso touching a 4-1/2-year peak, in reaction to a broad sell-off in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight.  \par \par \uc2 Renewed strength in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  triggered a wave of comments from officials. South Korea warned against won strength and the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it may relax its capital controls further to help ease upward pressure on the baht.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength was suspected in \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  and India.  \par \par \uc2 Trade was generally subdued with U.S. and Japanese markets closed for a holiday. But with the dollar taking a beating overnight as investors adjusted positions ahead of the break, Asia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets held their firm tone.  \par \par \uc2 "Over the last few weeks we have seen bouts of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on some \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while some central banks have said they are not concerned about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength," said Callum Henderson, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Standard Chartered Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "But the bias is for further Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength and we have had a major move in the dollar in the last 24 hours, albeit on thin liquidity."  \par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso <PHP=> rose to 44.66 to the dollar, its highest level in about 4-\u189\'00\'BD years, while the Singapore dollar <SGD=> extended Wednesday's gains to a new nine-year high of about 1.5520 per U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> rose to 7.8575 per dollar, the strongest since its July 2005 revaluation, while the Japanese yen <JPY=> was at 116.58 per dollar, up about 0.75 percent from late Wednesday's levels in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 SPOTLIGHT ON WON  \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won <KRW=> added as much as 0.5 percent to about 929.20 per dollar -- its highest in just over 1-\u189\'00\'BD weeks.  \par \par \uc2 It was supported by a South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decision on Thursday to raise reserve requirements on short-term deposits.  \par \par \uc2 The chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  official at South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned the bank would take steps whenever necessary to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, adding the won had overshot fair value.  \par \par \uc2 "It is more a case of the authorities wanting not only just to stem won strength because of concerns about exporters but also because it is starting to detect that speculative flows are behind won gains," said Bank of America \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Christy Tan.  \par \par \uc2 The won by some measures was still at record highs, raising concerns about export competitiveness, Tan said.  \par \par \uc2 The won gapped higher at Thursday's opening -- a sign of market strength, according to technical analysts.  \par \par \uc2 In Singapore, dealers said they did not suspect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap gains in the Singapore dollar despite market wariness in early trade about such action.  \par \par \uc2 A trader in Manila said it also appeared that the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had stayed away from the market as weakness in local stocks helped limit the peso's rally.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think they (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) have been in the market," he said. "One reason for the peso high is the major U.S. dollar sell-off overnight, but there is some weakness in the stock market, so the factors are balancing out."  \par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, Miranda Goeltom, Bank Indonesia's senior deputy governor, said the current exchange rate of the Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> was still conducive for the country's exports and imports. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0753 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       116.64         117.44       +0.69\par  Sing dlr        1.5532         1.5567       +0.23\par  Taiwan dlr      32.785         32.812       +0.08\par  Korean won      930.30         933.80       +0.38\par  Baht             36.53          36.58       +0.14\par  Peso             49.68          49.74       +0.11\par  Rupiah         9126.00        9130.00       +0.04\par  Rupee            44.71          44.80       +0.21\par  Ringgit         3.6360         3.6420       +0.17\par  Yuan            7.8590         7.8638       +0.06\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       116.64         117.96       +1.13\par  Sing dlr        1.5532         1.6625       +7.04\par  Taiwan dlr      32.785         32.850       +0.20\par  Korean won      930.30        1011.60       +8.74\par  Baht             36.53          41.11      +12.54\par  Peso             49.68          53.09       +6.86\par  Rupiah        