\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Markets further increase Asian  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  long positions  \b0\par\par\uc2 463 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 2006\par 04:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Nov 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets raised their long positions on the Singapore dollar and South Korean won and remained bullish on the Indonesian rupiah and Thai baht in the past couple of weeks, undeterred by sporadic \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a Reuters poll shows.  \par \par \uc2 The twice-monthly survey asked 15 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists to estimate how the market is positioned in four Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 It measures estimates on the net long or short position in a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a scale of minus 3 to plus 3. A score of plus 3 indicates the market is significantly long on dollars.  \par \par \uc2 The findings of the survey conducted on Nov. 14 are as follows:  \par \par \uc2 -- SOUTH KOREAN WON <KRW=>:  \par \par \uc2 The average positioning was minus 1.33, indicating the market had increased its short dollar positions versus the won in early November, having reversed a long dollar position in the previous two weeks. The scores ranged between zero and minus 2 with one respondent saying the market was neutral.  \par \par \uc2 -- SINGAPORE DOLLAR <SGD=>:  \par \par \uc2 The average positioning was minus 1.77, suggesting the market has ratcheted up long Singapore dollar positions against the U.S. dollar. The scores ranged between minus 1 and minus 3.  \par \par \uc2 -- INDONESIAN RUPIAH <IDR=>:  \par \par \uc2 The average positioning was minus 0.63, implying the market had slightly pared its short dollar-long rupiah positions. Scores ranged from minus 2 to zero.  \par \par \uc2 -- THAI BAHT <THB=>:  \par \par \uc2 The average positioning score was minus 1.67, almost the same level of long baht positions as estimated in the Oct. 31 poll. Scores ranged from zero to minus 3.  \par \par \uc2 Several Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit multi-month or multi-year highs versus the dollar this week, underpinned by foreign equity investment flows into Asia, softer U.S. economic data and talk that China was diversifying its estimated $1 trillion in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 Central banks in \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 , India and Thailand were suspected of having \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the gains in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Widespread U.S. dollar underperformance, coupled with steady gains in the yuan, has supported Asian regionals on a broad basis," said Sue Trinh, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at RBC Capital Markets.  \par \par \uc2 "We are seeing modest consolidation today after the hefty \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  especially by Bank of Korea early this week but, on a relative basis, Asia is still performing well," she said.  \par \par \uc2 ----------------------------------------------------  \par \par \uc2 SURVEY FINDINGS:  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  DATE       USD/KRW   USD/SGD   USD/IDR   USD/THB\par  14-11-06     -1.33     -1.77     -0.63     -1.67\par  31-10-06     -0.53     -1.09     -1.06     -1.75\par  16-10-06     +0.63     -0.34     -0.50     -0.50\par  ------------------------------------------------------\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For previous survey results, click on <ASIAFXPOLL>.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  (POLL)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|IF|Z|J  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061115e2bf0007b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
