\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korean won falls again on new  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk  \b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2006\par 01:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Nov 14 (Reuters) - The South Korean won <KRW=> slid against the dollar for a second session on Tuesday, ignoring the yen's <JPY=> spurt after what dealers suspected was more dollar buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the authorities to weaken the local unit.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased dollars for a second day on Tuesday after buying $1 billion on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday, dealers reported, worried the won's <KRW=> relentless rise to almost nine-year highs would hit the country's exports, which already face a slowing U.S. economy.  \par \par \uc2 The won settled domestic trade at 937.1 dollar, compared to the previous close of 934.8. In the prior session, the won hit a six-month high of 927.8 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "The government showed it would not tolerate further sharp gains of the won, even though its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today was not as strong as yesterday," a bank dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The yen rallied on Tuesday after data showed Japan's economy grew more rapidly than expected in the third quarter, keeping the Bank of Japan on track to raise interest rates in the next few months. [ID:nT121]  \par \par \uc2 Japan's gross domestic product expanded at a 2 percent annual rate in the July-September quarter, double forecasts, while growth for the previous quarter was revised up to a 1.5 percent annualised pace from 1.0 percent previously.  \par \par \uc2 On the economic front, South Korean import prices in won terms fell 1.4 percent in October from a year earlier, posting their first annual loss in one and a half years, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese yen <JPY=> was last quoted at 117.52/56 per dollar, from 118.14/16 in late New York trade the previous session.  \par \par \uc2 Seoul's main stock index <.KS11> closed up 0.76 percent, with foreign investors buying a net 61.4 billion won worth of shares on the main board.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                     0740 GMT     0320 GMT   prev close\par  Won <KRW=>               937.1    937.5/8.1        934.8\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>   7.9709/68    7.9655/48       7.9093\par  KOSPI <.KS11>         1,407.37     1,405.16     1,396.69\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061117e2be00012\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
