\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-S.Korea says missile launch won't hurt economy  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Yoo Choonsik  \par \uc2 593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2006\par 01:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Recasts after meeting ends, updates markets)  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, July 5 (Reuters) - South Korean officials said they did not expect a missile launch by North Korea on Wednesday to have much impact on the South's economy, but they were concerned that financial markets might overreact.  \par \par \uc2 Share prices and the won fell in early trade on worries the incident could dampen investors' confidence in Asia's fourth-largest economy, already faced with growing pessimism among consumers and companies.  \par \par \uc2 North Korea launched at least six missiles, including a long-range Taepodong 2 that appeared to fail in flight, U.S. officials said. See [ID:nL0465618] for details.  \par \par \uc2 Vice Finance Minister Bahk Byong-won told reporters after a meeting of senior economic policy makers the incident could slow down an improvement in South Korea's credit rating outlook but would not lead to an immediate change in the ratings themselves.  \par \par \uc2 Bahk said participants at the meeting, including the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deputy governor, had agreed to set up an emergency team to monitor financial markets before deciding whether to take measures.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think this will have any direct influence on the overall economy, although it may hurt the sentiment of investors, and the government has no plan at present to take any specific steps," Bahk told reporters.  \par \par \uc2 "If you look back on what happened in 1998, financial markets regained stability pretty soon after some turbulence in the early days," Bahk said, referring to a North Korean missile test-launch that year that sparked falls in markets in South Korea and elsewhere in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> lost just 0.1 percent to 944.5 per dollar in morning trade and reaction was also muted on Seoul's stock market, with the KOSPI <.KS11> down 0.49 percent at 0202 GMT, having fallen 2 percent at the start.  \par \par \uc2 "The missile launch is certainly a negative factor, but the effects should be limited to the short term ... This kind of drop is the least that can be expected in the situation," said Lim Chang-gue, a fund manager at Samsung Investment Trust Management.  \par \par \uc2 Bond prices edged up, with the five-year treasury bond yield <KR5YT=RR> offered three basis points lower at 4.97 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Chin Dong-soo, the second vice finance minister in charge of international affairs, told reporters \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets could temporarily show some instability and said the government would take steps if necessary.  \par \par \uc2 He did not elaborate, but \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the past when the won has moved wildly, although it has loosened its grip on the market of late.  \par \par \uc2 International credit rating agencies have said military tensions with the communist North were the single most important factor hurting South Korea's ratings. The two Koreas have remained technically at war since their 1950-53 conflict.  \par \par \uc2 "The test could delay a sovereign ratings upgrade of South Korea by Moody's, since the containment of the North Korea risk was one of the agency's criteria for an upgrade," said Dominique Dwor-Frecaut, an economist at Barclays Capital in Singapore, in a research report.  \par \par \uc2 The missile launch comes at a time when data is showing consumers and companies growing more pessimistic about the economic outlook as global oil prices remain high and a recovery in domestic demand fails to pick up pace. (Additional reporting by Lee Shin-hyung)  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-KOREA-NORTH (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060704e2740019f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
