\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  as won, Sing dlr hit 8-year highs  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Rajat Bhattacharya  \par \uc2 809 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Mai 2006\par 05:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, May 3 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of South Korea, Singapore and Malaysia hit their highest levels in more than eight years on Wednesday, prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the U.S. dollar fell on speculation U.S. interest rates would stop rising soon.  \par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> hit a high of 933.2 per dollar, its strongest level since October 1997.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> rose as high as 1.5730 per dollar, its highest since November 1997, while the Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> hit 3.6049 per dollar, a level last seen in April 1998.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said central banks across the region stepped in with dollar purchases to stifle further gains in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Some central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state lenders.  \par \par \uc2 "The state-run banks have been buying dollars aggressively," said a Singapore \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a foreign bank.  \par \par \uc2 The dealer said investors held off from bidding the Singapore dollar higher after seeing the authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 1.5730/35 levels. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could retreat to levels around 1.58 before traders pushed it higher again, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Similar \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was noted in \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Malaysia and Thailand.  \par \par \uc2 Asian authorities are worried that stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , could hurt Asian exports to the United States, Europe and Japan, particularly when China is keeping the yuan on a tight leash.  \par \par \uc2 Data on Wednesday indicated that the South Korean authorities had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since April. The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves jumped $5.55 billion last month to $222.89 billion, the fourth largest in the world.  \par \par \uc2 "The authorities are afraid of the pace and further appreciation of the won. That's why they came into the market to support the dollar. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- they want to moderate the pace and not stop the trend," said Roh Sang Chil, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Kookmin Bank in Seoul.  \par \par \uc2 Swiss bank UBS said concerns about the record U.S. current account deficit, attempts by central banks to diversify their reserves away from the dollar and expectations that the Fed may end its rate-rise cycle after another increase this month were likely to dominate \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 It expects the yen <JPY=> to strengthen to 108 per dollar in three months from about 113.25 now. The euro <EUR=> could climb to $1.3 from about $1.26 over the same period, it said.  \par \par \uc2 TAIWAN INFLOWS  \par \par \uc2 The bearish dollar outlook and a surge in foreign investment in Taiwan's stock market helped push up the Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> to a nine-month high of 31.59 per U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign investors continued with their purchases of Taiwan stocks, picking up a net T$11.7 billion worth on Wednesday. They bought T$170 billion worth in April, the highest monthly total since December.  \par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso <PHP=> jumped more than half a percent to 51.32 per dollar, its strongest level in two weeks.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had tumbled to an eight-week low last week on concern about record high oil prices and the likely impact on the country's fiscal deficit but some analysts reasoned that strong remittances from overseas Filipino workers were likely to offset the outflow of dollars caused by soaring crude oil import costs. New York oil futures <CLc1> traded close to $75 per barrel, near last week's record high of $75.35.  \par \par \uc2 Financial markets in Japan and China are shut for holidays for the rest of the week. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the day at   0821 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       113.35         113.80       +0.40\par  Sing dlr        1.5743         1.5797       +0.34\par  Taiwan dlr      31.616         31.786       +0.54\par  Korean won      934.10         940.10       +0.64\par  Baht             37.57          37.69       +0.32\par  Peso             51.27          51.60       +0.64\par  Rupiah         8775.00        8785.00       +0.11\par  Rupee            44.87          44.89       +0.03\par  Ringgit         3.6080         3.6135       +0.15 Change so\par far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       113.35         117.96       +4.07\par  Sing dlr        1.5743         1.6625       +5.60\par  Taiwan dlr      31.616         32.850       +3.90\par  Korean won      934.10        1011.60       +8.30\par  Baht             37.57          41.11       +9.42\par  Peso             51.27          53.09       +3.55\par  Rupiah         8775.00        9835.00      +12.08\par  Rupee            44.87          45.04       +0.37\pa