\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves rise amid  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk  \b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 2006\par 23:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, April 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose $1.21 billion during the first half of April, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Tuesday, amid talk the authorities had bought dollars in a bid to contain a rising won <KRW=>.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea said in a statement the reserves, which rank fourth in the world after China, Japan and Taiwan, rose to $218.55 billion by April 15 from $217.34 billion at the end of March due to investment gains.  \par \par \uc2 An official refused to comment on talk among dealers that the authorities actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market early this month, when the won rallied to its highest in eight years and a half against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Central banks usually do not comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  often admits to "smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", which it says are aimed at keeping the won from moving due to speculative trading, but would not say whether authorities are targeting a particular rate.  \par \par \uc2 The won gained 2.4 percent against the dollar during the first five trading days in April before falling back slightly. It is now trading up about 6 percent so far this year.  \par \par \uc2 Policy makers are worried a firmer won could hurt exports, although government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have recently appeared to be showing more tolerance over the won's strength.  \par \par \uc2 Rhee Yeung-kyun, an assistant governor at the Bank of Korea, said on Monday a firmer won has had little impact on exports so far, with exporters such as ship builders maintaining good orders.  \par \par \uc2 South Korea, Asia's fourth-largest economy, is home to global suppliers of microchips, mobile phones and ships such as Samsung Electronics Co. Ltd. , LG Electronics Inc. and Hyundai Heavy Industries Co. .  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said the Bank of Korea might stop releasing mid-month figures from as early as May, in line with previous comments by the finance ministry.  \par \par \uc2 South Korea's foreign reserves ($ billion):   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  mid-April  end-March  mid-March  end-Feb    mid-Feb    end-Jan\par  218.553    217.344    216.470    215.950    216.379    216.933\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-KOREA-RESERVES (URGENT)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060417e24h001ba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
