\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won hit highest in over 8 years, govt warns  \b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2006\par 02:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, April 6 (Reuters) - The South Korean won <KRW=> hit its highest in 8 and a half years against the dollar on Thursday, lifted by heavy foreign buying of local equities, prompting a government warning against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent surge.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  was prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if there were abnormal signs such as speculative trading, Vice Finance Minister Bahk Byong-won told a news conference. [ID:nSEO296172]  \par \par \uc2 The won finished local trade at 953.5, up 0.4 percent from Wednesday's domestic close of 957.3 per dollar. It hit 951.6 at one point, its strongest since touching 950 on Oct. 30, 1997.  \par \par \uc2 The won had earlier slipped as far as 962 after a government source told Reuters South Korea's finance minister and the new \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor met early on Thursday and discussed the won's recent sharp rise, raising concern of possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nSEO284513]  \par \par \uc2 "Dollar selling by exporters and offshore players outweighed some purchases by importers," a bank dealer said. "But the won will face some resistance to strengthen beyond the key 950 per dollar level."  \par \par \uc2 Data early on Thursday showed South Korea's consumer expectations index fell slightly for a third consecutive month in March, reinforcing concerns that a pick-up in domestic demand had faltered. [ID:nSEV000093]  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was quoted at 117.54/57, up from 116.95/97 in late Asian trade on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Investors are awaiting the Bank of Korea's decision on interest rates on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The Seoul stock market <.KS11> closed up 0.59 percent, gaining for an eleventh consecutive session, with foreign investors buying a net 125.5 billion won ($131.1 million) worth of shares on the main exchange by midday.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                     0620 GMT    0245 GMT   prev close\par  Won                      953.5   953.0/3.6        957.3\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>   8.1071/09   8.1125/06    8.1903/64\par  NDF 1-mth won        952.4/3.4   952.1/3.1    956.2/7.2\par  NDF 3-mth won        951.1/2.1   950.8/1.8    955.0/6.0\par  KOSPI                 1,397.00    1,389.69     1,388.77\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060409e2460000f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
