17.41/44, up from 116.95/97 in late Asian trade on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 - Investors awaiting the Bank of Korea's decision on interest rates on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 - The Seoul stock market <.KS11> up 0.07 percent, gaining for an eleventh consecutive session, with foreign investors buying a net 93.2 billion won ($97.36 million) worth of shares on the main exchange by midday.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                     0245 GMT    0012 GMT   prev close\par  Won                  953.0/3.6   959.7/0.2        957.3\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>   8.1125/06   8.1506/61    8.1903/64\par  NDF 1-mth won        952.1/3.1   958.9/9.7    956.2/7.2\par  NDF 3-mth won        950.8/1.8   957.5/8.5    955.0/6.0\par  KOSPI                 1,389.69    1,394.03     1,388.77\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060409e2460000e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
