\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea foreign reserves edge down by mid-Feb  \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2006\par 21:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Feb 17 (Reuters) - South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves edged lower during the first 15 days of February due to the dollar's rise against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the period, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which are the world's fourth largest, fell to $216.38 billion by Feb. 15 from $216.93 billion at the end of January, the Bank of Korea said in a statement.  \par \par \uc2 A firmer dollar cuts the value of assets held in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when converted into the U.S. unit. The euro <EUR=> fell 1.5 percent against the dollar, while the yen <JPY=> was barely changed over the period, according to Reuters data.  \par \par \uc2 "The decline was due to a reduced dollar-converted value of assets held in euro and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea does not release a breakdown of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its portfolio.  \par \par \uc2 The data is closely watched because a sharp rise in reserves can indicate dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by the authorities seeking to influence the won <KRW=>.  \par \par \uc2 South Korean authorities have purchased more than $1 billion per day on occasions when the won rose sharply, according to dealers, although neither the government nor the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  generally comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The won lost 1 percent during the first 15 days of February against the U.S. dollar, indicating authorities may have refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  actively in the market over the period.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves ($ billion):   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  mid-Feb   end-Jan   mid-Jan   end-Dec   mid-Dec   end-Nov\par  216.379   216.933   214.665   210.391   209.998   208.230\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-KOREA-RESERVES (EMBARGOED)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060216e22g0025e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
