\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-S.Korea vows to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  to smooth won rise  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Oh Jung-hwa  \par \uc2 650 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2006\par 01:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds Lotte source, updates market in paragraphs 9-12)  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Feb 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  pledged on Tuesday to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth a rally in the won <KRW=>, which the finance ministry says poses a growing risk to the country's economic growth along with high oil prices.  \par \par \uc2 Vice Finance Minister Kwon Tae-shin said the government was obliged to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moved rapidly. He was speaking hours after another official at the ministry said the government might take stabilising measures.  \par \par \uc2 Kwon also told a television programme the country's monetary policy should be maintained because of lingering risks facing Asia's fourth-largest economy, such as the firmer won and weak investment.  \par \par \uc2 The remarks came as data showed producer prices grew by their fastest annual pace in nine months in January, two days before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reviews interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 "The government is obliged to stabilise the market if the exchange rate shows an excessive volatility," Kwon, who was a deputy minister in charge of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy between 2003 and 2004, said during the television programme.  \par \par \uc2 A stronger won helps cap domestic inflation by cushioning higher global oil prices, but surprisingly slow growth in January exports has renewed worries about the more direct impact of the won's strength on economic growth.  \par \par \uc2 "The won's rise is due to the solid economic performance and healthy exports. But the government will conduct smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the market is tilted to one side," Kwon said.  \par \par \uc2 Kwon Tae-kyun, head of the ministry's international finance bureau, told Reuters early on Tuesday the government would take measures when necessary to cap the won's rise, a remark that was followed by what traders suspected was dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 LOTTE IPO MONEY  \par \par \uc2 As the voices of concern swirled, a source at South Korea's Lotte Shopping Co. told Reuters later it did not plan to bring in all the proceeds from its overseas initial public offering so as not to influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 The remark came as the won has been strongly supported by expectations for a heavy dollar supply from the department store chain's $3.54 billion IPO, as 80 percent of the shares offered were sold abroad.  \par \par \uc2 "We have sufficient time to exchange the proceeds as we have no immediate demand for money, so we will manage the process in such a manner as not to impact the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said the source by telephone.  \par \par \uc2 The won rose to hit an eight-year high of 957 per dollar on Feb. 1, before falling back slightly to 967.8 by the close of domestic trade on Tuesday, up 4.5 percent from the end of 2005.  \par \par \uc2 But on interest rate policy, Vice Minister Kwon made clear that should be decided by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Analysts were evenly split on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would raise interest rates or leave them unchanged at its Thursday policy meeting, but all agreed the rates would increase once or twice in the next six months, a Reuters poll showed on Monday.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data underlined rising inflation pressures, as the producer price index rose 2.1 percent in January from a year earlier, the fastest annual gain in nine months.  \par \par \uc2 Other data from the National Statistical Office showed annual growth in consumption spending per South Korean household accelerated in the fourth quarter from the third, in line with growing household income.  \par \par \uc2 Both the finance ministry and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have forecast South Korea's economic growth will accelerate to 5 percent this year from 4 percent in 2005, driven by recovering domestic demand and underpinned by resilient exports. (Additional reporting by Lee Shin-hyung, Lee Soo-jung)  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|ABX|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060207e227000p2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
