\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-INTERVIEW-S.Korean ratings could rise despite N.Korea  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Yoo Choonsik  \par \uc2 669 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Januar 2006\par 06:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, details)  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Jan 26 (Reuters) - South Korea's credit ratings could be raised even before the North Korean nuclear crisis is resolved, if the South makes progress on structural economic reforms, an S&P official said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Takahira Ogawa, a credit analyst at Standard & Poor's Ratings Services, also told Reuters in a telephone interview that the South Korean government's suspected resumption of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market would not affect its ratings.  \par \par \uc2 The agency raised the country's long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating by one notch to A in July last year, citing increased flexibility in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy along with an improved financial industry.  \par \par \uc2 It has since said that North Korea's nuclear ambitions remained the key constraint on the South's ratings.  \par \par \uc2 "Still, there is a chance (of an upgrade) even if the North Korean situation doesn't change that much," Ogawa said.  \par \par \uc2 "If the government could achieve or facilitate an environment in which the private sector can ensure more market-oriented competition, then perhaps we have a good chance of seeing higher ratings for Korea," he added.  \par \par \uc2 Talks involving the two Koreas, the United States, China, Russia and Japan produced an agreement in September last year on dismantling the North's nuclear programmes but follow-up talks have since hit snags.  \par \par \uc2 The July upgrade, the first for South Korea in three years, put the country's ratings at five notches above investment grade and above China and Malaysia at A-minus.  \par \par \uc2 Moody's Investors Service has an A3 rating on \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  while Fitch Ratings puts it at A-plus.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The South Korean authorities are believed to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  massively to cap the won <KRW=> <KRW=KFTC>, which has jumped since December to hit eight-year highs against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves soared by $4.27 billion in the first 15 days of January, a rise attributed by analysts mainly to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "This year they started to do it again, but until then, they were quite patient," Ogawa said of the suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "At this stage I still think their stance is changing," he added, meaning he believed the authorities, even if they \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would not do so as heavily as they did two years ago.  \par \par \uc2 Ogawa also said a possible slowdown in the U.S. economy could be the biggest risk to economic growth in South Korea this year, more so than won strength or high oil prices.  \par \par \uc2 "I think a slowdown in the U.S. or the global economy could be the strongest factor," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "(South Korea is) less vulnerable to fluctuations in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, in part because companies like Samsung, Hyundai Motor and so on started to establish or have already completely established their brand image," he added.  \par \par \uc2 South Korea is Asia's fourth-largest economy and home to Samsung Electronics Co. Ltd. , the world's largest maker of computer memory chips and the second biggest producer of flat screens, as well as car maker Hyundai Motor Co. Ltd. .  \par \par \uc2 Commenting on a domestic controversy about tax increases, Ogawa said steep tax rises would put a significant dent in consumer sentiment, which is recovering from a protracted slump.  \par \par \uc2 "If the government tries to move ahead with substantial tax increases, that could hurt sentiment in the economy more than, for example, one more round of interest rate increases by the Bank of Korea," he said.  \par \par \uc2 President Roh Moo-hyun said on Wednesday he would not seek to increase taxes sharply, a comment made in response to suspicions the government wanted to raise taxes to fund welfare spending.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea raised interest rates twice in the fourth quarter of 2005 to head off inflation and economists expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lift borrowing costs further this year.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-KOREA-RATINGS (INTERVIEW, UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|NAT  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060129e21q0001w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
