\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Edge down, rally on hold for now  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Dhara Ranasinghe  \par \uc2 826 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2006\par 03:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Jan 17 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased on Tuesday, hurt by a slowdown in foreign buying of local stocks and a view that an early 2006 rally in the regionals against the U.S. dollar had got ahead of itself.  \par \par \uc2  A perception that U.S. interest rates are close to reaching a peak has bolstered Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the start of the year. But dealers said with little new leads to drive regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher, some profit-taking had now set in.  \par \par \uc2  "Our short-term positioning indicators suggest the gains in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are overstretched and that more positive news would be needed for the rally to continue," said Shahab Jalinoos, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN AMRO. "Equity inflows were one factor but it looks like these are easing off as well."  \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar <TWD=> and Thai baht <THB=> both shed about half a percent against the U.S. dollar, while the Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> fell about 1 percent to 9,550 per dollar -- its softest level in more than a week.  \par \par \uc2  The yen also <JPY=> hit is lowest level in more than a week,  weighing on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although it had recovered some ground by late Asian trade.  \par \par \uc2  Foreign buying in Asian equity markets has eased in the past week, denting the appeal of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said.  \par \par \uc2  Indonesia's benchmark stock index <.JKSE> fell as much as 2.5 percent on Tuesday, while data from Nomura International showed heavy foreign selling of Indian and Korean equities in the past week.  \par \par \uc2  "There has been profit-taking in equity markets in Asia in recent sessions and there have been signs of a slowdown in foreign buying," said Craig Chan, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at the Royal Bank of Scotland in Hong Kong.  \par \par \uc2  Some traders, however, said Asian equity markets were likely to perform well over the next few months, and that should bode well for regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  "The overall fundamental story is still positive for Asia and over the long term we should see money flowing into the equity markets," one trader in Singapore said.  \par \par \uc2  DATA LIFTS SING DOLLAR  \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar <SGD=> hit a session high at 1.6303 per U.S. dollar, paring earlier falls, after the government said growth in non-oil exports would not be curbed by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength and data showed a sharp rise in exports.  \par \par \uc2  Singapore's non-oil exports rose 18 percent in December from November on a seasonally adjusted basis, much higher than the 1.0 percent increase forecast by analysts.  \par \par \uc2  "There are definitely some flows coming in after the data," a trader said. "The Singapore dollar has strengthened since the end of last year and this is in line with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's view of a gradual appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The economy is doing better and this does justify a stronger Sing dollar."  \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won <KRW=><KRW=KFTC> weakened as much as 0.8 percent from Monday's domestic close to 990.3 per dollar, moving further away from last week's 8-year high at about 973.8.  \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they remained wary about possible dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb recent won strength, especially after \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve figures suggested the authorities had been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose $4.27 billion in the first 15 days of January, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data on Tuesday showed. It was the biggest gain in South Korea's foreign reserves for a half-month period since a $4.66 billion rise in the first half of March 2005, an official at the Bank of Korea said.  Change on the day at 0822 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       114.73         114.34       -0.34\par  Sing dlr        1.6307         1.6273       -0.21\par  Taiwan dlr      31.990         31.927       -0.20\par  Korean won      988.90         982.50       -0.65\par  Baht             39.70          39.61       -0.23\par  Peso             52.56          52.58       +0.04\par  Rupiah         9470.00        9440.00       -0.32\par  Rupee            44.30          44.21       -0.19\par  Ringgit         3.7490         3.7420       -0.19\par  Yuan            8.0665         8.0660       -0.01\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       114.73         117.96       +2.82\par  Sing dlr        1.6307         1.6625       +1.95\par  Taiwan dlr      31.990         32.850       +2.69\par  Korean won      988.90        1011.60       +2.30\par  Baht             39.70          41.11       +3.55\par  Peso             52.56          53.09       +1.01\par  Rupiah         9470.00        9835.00       +3.85\par  Rupee            44.30          45.04       +1.68\par  Ringgit         3.7490         3.7790       +0.80\par  Yuan            8.0665         8.0702       +0.05\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|Z|IF|PHD|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060120e21h0006x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
