\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won rises on yen despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  talk  \b0\par\par\uc2 418 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2006\par 02:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  (Updates to midday)  \par \par \uc2  0320 GMT - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's won <KRW=> rises 0.5 percent on offshore buying and a firmer yen <JPY=>, but gains capped by sporadic dollar buying suspected to be coming from authorities.  \par \par \uc2  - Won <KRW=KFTC> quoted at 982.6 per dollar, up 0.52 percent from Friday's domestic close of 987.8. It opened at 983.0.  \par \par \uc2  - Won fell about 1.5 percent on Friday, with dealers estimating more than $1 billion spent by authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the finance minister pledged to curb the won's strength.  \par \par \uc2  - Authorities appear to be continuing dollar purchases, but only on a limited scale, dealers say.  \par \par \uc2  - "Some smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the won's gains kept the dollar above 980," said a dealer at a domestic bank. "Sentiment for the dollar remains weak as the U.S. unit is weakening globally."  \par \par \uc2  - The Bank of Korea does not confirm or comment on its actual dealings in the market but has said it will launch "smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 " if necessary.  \par \par \uc2  - Dollar under pressure after U.S. retail sales and core producer prices weaker than expected. Traders questioning how much further the Federal Reserve will raise interest rates after the sluggish data.  \par \par \uc2  - Yen, which the won closely follows due to competition between exporters from the two countries, last quoted at 114.11/14 per dollar from 114.60/62 late on Friday in Asia.  \par \par \uc2  - Dealers expect the won to trade between 973-994.4 this week, according to 10 dealers surveyed by Reuters.  \par \par \uc2  - The market shows little reaction to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief's comments that monetary policy this year will focus on pre-empting inflation and supporting economic growth.  \par \par \uc2  - Bank of Korea Governor Park Seung said the surging won and high oil prices key risks for the economy. [nSEV000038]  \par \par \uc2  - Seoul's benchmark stock price index <.KS11> flat, with foreigners selling a net 105.8 billion won in shares on the main board.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                      0320 GMT      0055 GMT    prev close\par  Won <KRW=KFTC>            982.6         982.6         987.8\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R>    8.6030/20     8.6246/62     8.6129/20\par  NDF 1-mth won         981.4/2.4     981.9/2.9     986.9/7.9\par  NDF 3-mth won         980.6/1.6     981.1/2.1     986.1/7.1\par  KOSPI <.KS11>          1,416.56      1,412.68      1,416.28\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060119e21g0003c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
