\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Hitting new highs after a pause  \b0\par\par\uc2 783 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2006\par 03:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Jan 12 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit fresh multi-month highs against the dollar on Thursday as traders bet that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had further to fall after a brief consolidation early this week.  \par \par \uc2  Hawkish comments from the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , expectations that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would sound a hawkish note at a meeting later in the day and anxiety ahead of U.S. trade data all weighed on the dollar. It has already shed about 2.5 percent in trade-weighted terms <=USD> this month.  \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar <SGD=> rose to its highest level in nearly 10 months at about 1.6220 per U.S. dollar, and the Thai baht <THB=> rose to about 39.38 per dollar, its highest since May 2005.  \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won <KRW=><KRW=KFTC> strengthened more than one percent from Wednesday's domestic close to 973.8 per dollar, its strongest level since November 1997.  \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> also added more than one percent to its strongest level in almost 10 months, while the Taiwan dollar <TW1D=TP> firmed to 31.831 per U.S. dollar -- its highest level since early August.  \par \par \uc2  "There's been a lot of appreciation against the dollar but, the way these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are managed, I doubt there's been much trade-weighted appreciation," said Tim Condon, head of research at ING in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2  Callum Henderson, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Standard Chartered Bank, said that while there had been a huge move in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at the start of 2006, similar rapid moves in the early weeks of the past three years had not been sustained.  \par \par \uc2  "We will see some degree of consolidation. However, we are very much in the camp that believes in medium-term dollar weakness so any consolidation will be a further opportunity to offload more dollars," he said.  \par \par \uc2  WATCHFUL CENTRAL BANKS  \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht's rise versus the dollar has made it a "bit too strong" and its appreciation should require \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakul said on Thursday. "No one has confirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but everybody is talking about it," said a trader in Bangkok. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is worried that a strong baht is not good for exports so \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be a surprise."  \par \par \uc2  So far this month, \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  has warned against won strength, while Taiwan has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to curb Taiwan dollar strength.  \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) had been less aggressive than expected in its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap Sing dollar gains and this had encouraged some investors to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher.  \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar has risen nearly 3 percent in the past three weeks.  \par \par \uc2  "The entire street seems to be short Sing dollar against the basket," said a local trader.  \par \par \uc2  He said the U.S. dollar's weakness, driven by the view that U.S. monetary tightening was close to an end, had left those betting against the Sing dollar in the red and led to short-covering.  \par \par \uc2  "And with MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  only in bits and pieces, it is making life for those Sing dollar shorts pretty miserable."  \par \par \uc2  The MAS's chief monetary policy tool is the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which it manages within an undisclosed trade-weighted band against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0825 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       114.06         114.75       +0.60\par  Sing dlr        1.6237         1.6348       +0.68\par  Taiwan dlr      31.874         32.068       +0.61\par  Korean won      973.80         984.40       +1.09\par  Baht             39.43          39.87       +1.12\par  Peso             52.35          52.55       +0.38\par  Rupiah         9355.00        9460.00       +1.12\par  Rupee            44.14          44.29       +0.35\par  Ringgit         3.7405         3.7465       +0.16\par  Yuan            8.0659         8.0680       +0.03\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       114.06         117.96       +3.42\par  Sing dlr        1.6237         1.6625       +2.39\par  Taiwan dlr      31.874         32.850       +3.06\par  Korean won      973.80        1011.60       +3.88\par  Baht             39.43          41.11       +4.26\par  Peso             52.35          53.09       +1.41\par  Rupiah         9355.00        9835.00       +5.13\par  Rupee            44.14          45.04       +2.05\par  Ringgit         3.7405         3.7790       +1.03\par  Yuan            8.0659         8.0702       +0.05\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|