\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won dips amid  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  caution  \b0\par\par\uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 2005\par 01:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Dec 1 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's won fell on Thursday, as a string of upbeat U.S. economic data chilled sentiment for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and after a government official urged authorities to act to curb the won's strength versus the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Benign inflation data means the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would probably hold interest rates steady for a second consecutive month at its Dec. 8 policy meeting, dealers said, helping snap three days of gains for the local unit.  \par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=KFTC> <KRW=> fell 0.11 percent to 1,034.6 per dollar from Wednesday's domestic finish of 1,033.5, which was the strongest close in more than two months.  \par \par \uc2 Shin Dong-sik, director general of the commerce ministry's trade bureau, said authorities should take measures to curb the won's gains against Japan's yen, warning of an adverse impact on exports.  \par \par \uc2 South Korean exporters compete closely with their Japanese counterparts in several key sectors including chips, consumer goods and cars.  \par \par \uc2 The won climbed 5.8 percent against the yen in the past two months, compared with a 0.7 percent rise versus the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers also called on the government to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check the won's upswing.  \par \par \uc2 "Given the current supply and demand balance, the absence of authorities' \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will accelerate the won's strong trend," said Lee Jin-woo, an analyst of Nonghyup futures, in a research note.  \par \par \uc2 South Korea's annual consumer inflation was expected to slow to 2.7 percent this year from 3.6 percent in 2004, the finance ministry said, a week ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy meeting.  \par \par \uc2 In November, South Korea's inflation slowed to 2.4 percent from 2.5 percent in October, below market expectations.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, exports rose 13.0 percent to a record $26.07 billion last month from a year earlier, helping the country post a trade surplus of $2.13 billion, government data showed.  \par \par \uc2 South Korea's unemployment rate would probably fall to 3.4 percent in 2006 from an estimated 3.7 percent this year, Labour Minister Kim Dae-hwan said in a news conference.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers were also awaiting a rate setting meeting by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The ECB is widely expected to increase its key rate for the first time in five years.  \par \par \uc2 The yen <JPY=>, which the won usually follows closely, was quoted at 119.87/91 per dollar, versus 119.80 in late U.S. trade.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign investors were sellers of a net 22 billion won worth of local equities on the main exchange.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark stock index <.KS11> ended up 0.66 percent.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                  0722 GMT       0034 GMT     prev close\par  Won <KRW=KFTC>       1,034.6       1,034.0       1,033.5\par  Yen/won <JPYKRW=R> 8.6297/50     8.6324/77     8.6571/10\par  NDF 1-mth won    1,033.8/4.8   1,033.2/4.2   1,032.6/3.6\par  NDF 3-mth won    1,033.1/4.1   1,032.4/3.4   1,031.9/2.9\par  KOSPI <.KS11>       1,305.98    1,294.01      1,297.44\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051201e1c10001u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
