\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea worried about yen, but no  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Yoo Choonsik  \par \uc2 735 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 2005\par 08:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Nov 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to avoid a new round of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the strength of the won, which hit a seven-year high against the yen on Wednesday, for fear of fanning inflation, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 Finance ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have expressed concerns about the won's strength but dealers do not expect any massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to follow the rhetoric.  \par \par \uc2 A weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could mean a rise in import costs, which could increase the pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost interest rates again.  \par \par \uc2 "The finance ministry apparently doesn't like to see interest rates raised aggressively and so must be concerned about inflation," said Oh Suk-tae, an economist at Citibank.  \par \par \uc2 South Korean and Japanese exporters are major competitors in many markets, such as for autos and technology.  \par \par \uc2 The won gained 13 percent against the yen <JPYKRW=R> this year to hit 8.89 per yen on Wednesday, its strongest since August 1998. It has gained 5.6 percent in last two months alone.  \par \par \uc2 Rhee Gwang-ju, head of the Bank of Korea's international department, told Reuters on Wednesday the won had gained too much against the yen but would now reverse the trend.  \par \par \uc2 "(We) expect the bullish sentiment for the won to reverse to reflect the dollar's strength against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said, echoing a similar comment on Tuesday by the finance ministry's head of the international finance bureau, Kwon Tae-kyun.  \par \par \uc2 Traders, including Park Yong-il, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at DBS Bank's Seoul branch, shrugged off the comments.  \par \par \uc2 "If they meant to step in, they should have done it today," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The won's rise against the yen would make South Korean products more expensive relative to competing Japanese ones, even in dollar markets, although analysts said the impact may not be that great since importers also look at other factors, such as quality, rather than just price.  \par \par \uc2 "The government may want to smooth out the rise but the possibility is low because they know well the exchange rate is not very important in exports any longer," said Park.  \par \par \uc2 The yen/won rate is based on each \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value against the dollar. The won's rise against the yen has been the result of its slower depreciation against the dollar compared with the yen.  \par \par \uc2 So far this year, the yen has skidded more than 12 percent against the dollar, while the won has fallen less than 1 percent.  \par \par \uc2 "I think the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy has been to stay away," said Oh. "The won is strong not only against the yen but against many \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But I don't think the government can do something about this."  \par \par \uc2 FINANCE MINISTRY LESS HAWKISH  \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry decides when to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acts on its behalf in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 Hawkish finance ministry officials successfully kept the won flat versus the dollar in 2003 despite the yen's <JPY=> 11 percent rise and the euro's <EUR=> 20 percent increase against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But the won snapped back against the dollar, yen and euro last year. Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gyrations, exports have remained surprisingly resilient this year.  \par \par \uc2 South Korea's inflation has been relatively benign this year, largely the result of the won's strength last year which has helped offset the soaring import cost of crude oil -- the main factor fuelling inflation world wide.  \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry now appears concerned a weaker won would fan inflation, in turn forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise interest rates and dampen a nascent revival in consumer spending, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 "I think the finance ministry doesn't want to create a situation in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to raise interest rates," said Citibank's Oh.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates last month by a quarter percentage point from a record low of 3.25 percent for the first time in more than three years, citing future inflation pressure as a result of recovering domestic demand.  \par \par \uc2 The annual inflation rate remains low at below 3 percent, but persistently high global oil prices and a pick-up in domestic demand could fuel price pressures in coming months, analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-KOREA-YEN|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|J|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051102e1b2000jp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
