\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-INTERVIEW-S.Korea won seen capped vs dollar  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Yoo Choonsik and Lee Bong-hyun  \par \uc2 576 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2005\par 06:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes, more details, market)  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, Oct 19 (Reuters) - A narrowing trade surplus in South Korea and an upbeat trend in the dollar will cap the won for the rest of the year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's most senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Rhee Gwang-ju, director general at the Bank of Korea's international department, said in an interview he doubted the won's levels would have a serious impact on inflation.  \par \par \uc2 "Over the next quarter, for instance, it is difficult to find any factors for a strengthening won," Rhee said, adding the trade surplus could drastically shrink in line with recovering domestic demand.  \par \par \uc2 "There clearly is some upward pressure (on inflation) from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate but I don't think the impact will be serious," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Inflation was 2.7 percent in September, the highest since June.  \par \par \uc2 The won weakened slightly against the dollar after Rhee's comments. Analysts said the fact Rhee did not talk up the won suggested he saw no reason for the current weakening trend against the dollar to change.  \par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> <KRW=KFTC> has fallen 2.6 percent against a broadly strong dollar in the past month and is down 1.9 percent so far this year. It finished Wednesday's domestic session at 1,054.8 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 However, the won gained 15 percent against the dollar in 2004 to be Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The won's levels are critical for South Korea's exporters, which have provided the main economic growth for the country in recent years.  \par \par \uc2 But like many other Asian countries, Korea has taken a major hit on its import bill as crude prices soared, undermining the country's trade surplus, the won's levels and raising concerns about imported inflation.  \par \par \uc2 COMPETING  \par \par \uc2 Rhee brushed off concerns about the strength of the won against the yen, a cross rate closely monitored since Korea and Japan compete in similar export markets, such as for computer chips, ships, autos and steel.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think the yen/won rate's recent drop has become a trend or would continue for a long time," he said, adding sharp fluctuations in the cross rate were common.  \par \par \uc2 The yen has fallen 11.6 percent against the dollar, a much bigger decline compared with the won, which has allowed the Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to gain against the Japanese unit.  \par \par \uc2 The won was quoted at 9.11 per yen, up 12.5 percent from a 2005 low of 10.25 per yen on Jan. 14, Reuters data shows.  \par \par \uc2 Policy makers expressing concerns about the won's strength have unnerved investors in the past because Korean authorities have regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb a rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  actively this year.  \par \par \uc2 Rhee doubted heavy selling of Korean stocks by foreign investors was a "sell Korea" signal, suggesting instead it was profit-taking.  \par \par \uc2 Foreign investors were net sellers of South Korean shares for the 19th consecutive session on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Seoul's main stock index <.KS11> hit a record high earlier this month of 1,246.41, a gain of more than 70 percent over the previous 14 months. The index has fallen more than 6 percent since then. ($1=1053.0 Won)  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (INTERVIEW, UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051019e1aj00093\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
