\par\par \b \uc2 DJ S Korea Ctrl Bank Gov Rules Out  \highlight22\uc2 Currency Intervention \highlight\uc2  -FT  \b0\par\par\uc2 422 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 2005\par 22:05\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2005, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, May 18, 2005 (ODC via Comtex) --  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  any further in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the governor of the Bank of Korea said Wednesday, according to an article on the Web site of the Financial Times.  \par \par \uc2 "I believe that we now have sufficient reserves to secure our sovereign credibility, so I do not anticipate increasing the amount of foreign reserves further," Park Seung told the FT. South Korea's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stand at $206 billion, the fourth-largest in the world.  \par \par \uc2 Park told the newspaper: "We now need to take more consideration of profitability, and I think we're at a stage where we need to manage our reserves in a more useful way."  \par \par \uc2 Although he made no explicit comment on the won, Park's remarks imply that \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now unwilling to undertake the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  required to stem its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, the FT said.  \par \par \uc2 Park said he didn't envision changing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  mix of the country's reserves, about two-thirds of which is thought to be in dollar-denominated assets, the newspaper reports.  \par \par \uc2 With Japan, China and South Korea - which together hold at least a third of the world's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves - each likely to suffer if one moves first to lessen their exposure to the dollar, some economists believe there is scope for more regional cooperation.  \par \par \uc2 Park told the FT: "I think that the economic cooperation of these three nations and the cooperation of their central banks is necessary to promote the growth and development of the global economy."  \par \par \uc2 But the banks were working together only to maintain financial stability and weren't doing anything that might "affect" international markets, he told the newspaper.  \par \par \uc2 Regarding adjustments to China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Park told the FT that "I think that is China's job, (but) China is smart enough to deal with this issue to help adjust the imbalances within the global economy and stabilize the regional economy."  \par \par \uc2 Of greater concern to Park were the U.S.'s current account and budget deficits, which Asian central banks have largely been funding. The deficits "will aggravate the global imbalances and undermine global economic growth," Park said to the newspaper. "I think there is a need for the U.S. to dissolve these twin deficits for the benefit of the U.S. economy, the world economy and the Korean economy."  \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires  \par \par \uc2 05-18-05 1512ET  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020050518e15i00237\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
