\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-S.Korea has no plan to alter  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves - c.bank  \b0\par\par\uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 2005\par 01:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Updates with quotes and details)  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, May 19 (Reuters) - South Korean authorities have no plan to either increase or decrease \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official told Reuters on Thursday, in comments aimed at clarifying the country's stance on the sensitive issue.  \par \par \uc2 Rhee Gwang-ju, the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's international affairs bureau, also said by telephone that authorities were ready to take action if the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market showed signs of instability.  \par \par \uc2 The comments came after the Financial Times quoted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Park Seung as saying he did not anticipate the country would increase the amount of its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 "The Financial Times report carrying an interview with the governor was not correct. In case speculative money flows into the country based on reports that are different from facts, we will take firm action," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a later statement.  \par \par \uc2 The report helped push the dollar down against the yen to a session low of 106.76 yen <JPY=> in New York as dealers interpreted it to mean that there could be less dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Asian monetary authorities in the future.  \par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> <KRW=KFTC> opened domestic trade firmer at 999.5 per dollar, breaching the psychologically-important 1,000 mark. It traded at 1,001.7 at 0023 GMT, up 0.35 percent.  \par \par \uc2 "The governor's remarks meant that the country has a scope of flexibility on the reserve front but was not intended to hint that the authorities would not need to increase reserves or not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Rhee said.  \par \par \uc2 "We do not have a plan to artificially increase or decrease reserves," he added.  \par \par \uc2 Financial markets are especially sensitive to even the slightest hint of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  diversification out of dollar-denominated assets, particularly given intense speculation that China will soon make its exchange rate regime more flexible.  \par \par \uc2 Most analysts expect other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate against the dollar once China allows the yuan to strengthen.  \par \par \uc2 "I believe that we now have sufficient reserves to secure our sovereign credibility, so I do not anticipate increasing the amount of foreign reserves further," the Financial Times quoted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor as saying.  \par \par \uc2 "We now need to take more consideration of profitability, and I think we're at a stage where we need to manage our reserves in a more useful way," he added.  \par \par \uc2 Separately, Park told Reuters in an interview with Reuters on Wednesday that there were no immediate plans to change the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  composition of the country's huge \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 At around $207 billion, South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are the fourth-largest in the world.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea also took issue with part of the Financial Times report that said \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  any further in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and said in a statement that the governor had been "misinterpreted".  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will take action if the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market turns unstable", the statement added.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -WARNINGS (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ABX|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050519e15i0001g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
