\par\par \b \uc2 South Korea  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves edge down by mid-April.  \b0\par\par\uc2 350 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 2005\par 23:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, April 19 (Reuters) - South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves edged down in the first half of April, hit by a weakening in non-dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the U.S. unit during the period, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers also said that there had been little \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to build up reserves as the won fell 0.4 percent against the dollar in the first half of the month.  \par \par \uc2 The country's reserves, the fourth biggest in the world, dropped 0.1 percent to $205.2 billion as of April 15, from $205.4 billion at the end of March, the Bank of Korea said in a statement.  \par \par \uc2 Drops in the value of non-dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the euro reduced the dollar conversion of assets held in these \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the statement said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro dropped 0.35 percent against the dollar in the first half of April and the yen eased 0.67 percent for the same period.  \par \par \uc2 The latest data showed reserves have risen more than a quarter from a year before, although the figure was down from a record level of $206.82 billion on March 15.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a rare acknowledgement of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month that reserves hit a record high in mid-March, partly due to dollar buying to cap a rise in the won.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the local market last year to control the won's rise in order to help maintain the price competitiveness of its exports, currently the main plank supporting growth in the economy, Asia's third largest.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Despite this, the won             gained 15 percent against the dollar\par in 2004, and additional 1.5 percent so far this year.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean officials have blamed speculators for the recent surge in the won and said they would fight what they regard as abnormal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korean foreign reserves ($ billion):  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mid-April End-March End-Feb End-Jan End-Dec End-Nov  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 205.217 205.447 202.162 199.699 199.066 192.602.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050418e14i00gz5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
