\par\par \b \uc2 South Korea  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves rise 1.6 percent in March.  \b0\par\par\uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 April 2005\par 23:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SEOUL, April 4 (Reuters) - South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reserves rose $3.29 billion in March from February, bolstered\par by a big increase in the first half of the month from\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap a climb in the won, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  data\par showed on Monday.\par     The country's reserves, the fourth biggest in the world,\par rose to $205.45 billion at the end of March from $202.16\par billion a month before, the Bank of Korea said.\par     "The increase mainly came from the rise in the process of\par stabilising the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and gains from\par investment," the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in a statement.\par     It had previously been rare for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par acknowledge \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , although it had also said in the\par middle of March that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been behind the rise in\par reserves.\par     Some dealers have estimated the Bank of Korea bought as\par much as $2 billion on a single day in early March, when the won\par              was rising against the dollar.\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily in the local market\par last year to control the won's rise in order to help maintain\par the price competitiveness of its exports.\par  \par     Despite this, the won gained 15 percent against the dollar\par in 2004.\par     The latest data showed reserves have risen more than a\par quarter from a year before, although the figure was down from a\par record level of $206.82 billion on March 15.\par     An official at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  attributed this to a\par weakening in non-dollar \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during the second half of\par the month against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Drops in the value of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the yen        and\par the euro  against the dollar reduce the dollar conversion\par of assets held in these \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The yen and euro lost about 2.5 percent respectively to the\par U.S. dollar during the second half of March.\par     The Bank of Korea does not release a detailed make-up of\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in its reserves, but a senior official told Reuters  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 on March 30 the country had more non-dollar assets than many  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 other countries out of total reserves.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The Bank of Korea releases \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves\par figures twice a month.\par     South Korean foreign reserves ($ billion):\par  End-March  Mid-March    End-Feb    Mid-Feb    End-Jan\par Mid-Jan\par    205.447    206.815    202.162    200.249    199.699\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 199.241.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050403e14300dw3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
