\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 South Korea FX \highlight\uc2  reserves hit record on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kim Yeon-hee and Yoo Choonsik  \par \uc2 598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 08:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, March 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose $4.66 billion in the first 15 days of March to a new record, boosted by massive government \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap a soaring won, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea also announced in a separate statement it planned to increase its fund management team by around a half as part of efforts to boost returns on the country's reserves, the world's fourth largest.  \par \par \uc2 South Korea's reserves grew 2.3 percent to $206.82 billion as of March 15 from $202.16 billion at the end of February, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made a rare acknowledgement that dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by authorities aimed at containing a surge in the won was behind the increase.  \par \par \uc2 "In addition to increased foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets resulting from the process of stabilising the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the conversion value of existing reserves in euro and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has risen because of a weakening U.S. dollar," it said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's explicit reference to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared aimed at showing its determination to try and quell what it has called speculative trading driving up the won, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers in Seoul estimated some $3 billion of the increased reserves came from direct purchases by authorities in the market to cap the won, after the local unit soared to a seven-year high against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  late last week.  \par \par \uc2 The reserves, which fell to less than $4 billion during the 1997-98 Asian financial crisis, have jumped 16 percent since the end of October when the won \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  started rising sharply.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won            , a star performer in Asia with a 15 percent gain in\par 2004, has risen another 3 percent against the U.S. dollar over the year\par to date.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MORE MANAGERS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in another statement it wanted to raise the number of fund mangers as part of efforts to make the management of its reserves more profitable, a goal officials at the bank have been pursuing since reserves have kept growing.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The statement followed a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  report in late February that it would diversify its reserves into high yielding paper and a greater variety of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , though it later clarified the plan did not mean it would sell dollars to buy other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We have been making efforts to increase profitability from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves by investing them in wider areas, at the same time keeping in mind securing liquidity and stability of those assets," it said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would increase the number of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  asset managers to over 100 from the current 66.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "At a time where \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves are marking $200 billion, the Bank of Korea is seeking to revamp the management organisation and personnel of the reserves," the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A time-frame for the new appointments would be set in April, Won Jong-seok, an official at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  management division, told Reuters by telephone.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's returns on reserves were already relatively higher than those at other central banks and yields on global bonds, thanks to the upgrading of its reserves management systems and recruitment of professional managers.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's finance ministry also plans to launch a separate government agency later this year to invest an initial $20 billion of the country's reserves, targeting more aggressive investment returns.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050317e13h006de\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
