\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-S.Korea plays down Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  impact of yuan reform.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Lee Bong-hyun and Yoo Choonsik  \par \uc2 603 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 11:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, March 17 (Reuters) - South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , notably the won and Taiwan dollar, were unlikely to rise much more against the U.S. dollar, even if China revalued its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The remarks appeared to be another attempt by South Korean authorities to quell speculation in the won, which has risen sharply along with some other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  partly in expectation China will relax controls over the yuan, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Several Asian countries have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in markets to curb the strength of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , leaving their central banks with record \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 "Even if the yuan appreciates following the increased flexibility in the yuan system, it will not have a big impact on improving the trade balances (with) Asian countries and therefore will not likely play a role in sparking a follow-up appreciation of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in these countries," the Bank of Korea said in a report on international economic affairs.  \par \par \uc2 China and other Asian countries have come under pressure from the United States and Europe to allow their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate to address global current account imbalances.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the United States said its 2004 current account deficit hit a record equal to more than 6 percent of gross domestic product.  \par \par \uc2 China, with the world's fastest growing major economy, has faced most criticism to relax its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls that limit the yuan's movement to a razor-thin 8.276-8.28 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Beijing has resisted, saying reforms will be gradual.  \par \par \uc2 WON'T BE TOLERATED  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea said the won and Taiwan dollar have already appreciated considerably on the prospect of a yuan revaluation.  \par \par \uc2 "Even if the flexibility of the yuan is heightened, the scope of its appreciation is very likely to be limited within tolerable ranges due to possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the People's Bank of China," it said, referring to China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The won and the Taiwan dollar have risen 14 percent and 9 percent, respectively, against the U.S. dollar in the last five months.  \par \par \uc2 "Moreover, the scope of appreciation in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely be limited because each country is expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market when the appreciation pressure builds up on yen and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the yuan's appreciation," it said.  \par \par \uc2 Asian central banks have close to $2.5 trillion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in their coffers as a result of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sap the strength of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves rose $4.66 billion in the first half of March to more than $200 billion, while Taiwan's reserves were $247 billion at the end of February.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers in Seoul were sceptical of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's view, at least in the case of the won.  \par \par \uc2 "The won has appreciated a lot from its 2001 level but there is still some room for the won to go up further once the yuan is revalued," said Park Yong-il, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at DBS Bank's Seoul branch. "The remarks appear partly aimed at preventing a yuan revaluation from sparking a panic situation."  \par \par \uc2 The won has gained 32 percent since the end of 2001 against the U.S. dollar, while the Taiwan dollar is up 12.6 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Chinese Premier Wen Jiabao said on Monday Beijing could spring a surprise on markets in deciding when and how it reformed the yuan, a comment seen as a warning to speculators trying to profit from a rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050317e13h002ml\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
