\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves up by mid-March on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 22:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, March 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves grew 2.3 percent in the first half of March, boosted by dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by authorities to contain a surge in the won, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Korea also said in a statement that larger investment gains from non-dollar-denominated assets had lifted reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The country's reserves, the world's fourth-largest, rose to $206.82 billion as of March 15, from $202.16 billion at the end of February, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said.  \par \par \uc2 "In addition to increased foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets resulting from the process of stabilising the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the conversion value of existing reserves in euro and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  has risen because of a weakening U.S. dollar," it added, making rare comments about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dealers estimate South Korean authorities spent more than $3 billion buying dollars over the first 15 days of March, after the won soared to a seven-year high against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  early this month.  \par \par \uc2 South Korean policy makers have been keen to control rises in the won given the impact on price competitiveness of exports, currently the main plank supporting growth in the economy, Asia's third largest.  \par \par \uc2 South Korean officials have blamed speculators for the recent surge in the won and said they would fight what they regard as abnormal \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.  \par \par \uc2 The won , a star performer in Asia with a 15 percent gain in 2004, has risen another 3 percent so far this year against the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 South Korean foreign reserves ($ billion):  \par \par \uc2 Mid-March End-Feb End-Jan End-Dec End-Nov End-Oct  \par \par \uc2 206.815 202.162 199.699 199.066 192.602 178.388.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050316e13g00ada\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
