\par\par \b \uc2 S Korea  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Reserves Hit Record In Mar Due To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 206 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 22:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves climbed $4.65 billion in the first half of March to a record $206.82 billion due to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the authorities to curb the won's rise, the Bank of Korea said Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 In an unusually frank statement, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the reserves rose "in the process of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market stabilization."  \par \par \uc2 The BOK also attributed the increase to a rise in the value of its euro-denominated assets, which appreciated markedly when calculated in terms of the weakening U.S. dollar, and a rise in its operating profit.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers suspect authorities spent $2 billion on March 10 alone to prop up the dollar above KRW1,000. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell as low as KRW989.0 on that day after Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi said diversity in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves was necessary, as a general rule.  \par \par \uc2 The reserves rose $1.91 billion in the previous half-month period from mid-February to the end of last month.  \par \par \uc2 -By In Kyung Kim, Dow Jones Newswires; 822-732-2165; in-kyung.kim@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Hilary Mc Cully [ 16-03-05 2100GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050316e13g0010n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
