\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Taiwan dlr sets new 4-1/2-year high, baht falls.  \b0\par\par\uc2 715 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 09:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     SINGAPORE, March 3 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar reached\par its strongest level in over 4-1/2-years on Thursday after signs\par of easing tensions with China and a strong economy lifted\par foreigners' demand for the island's shares over the past month.\par     The Taiwan dollar gained as much as a fifth of a percent to\par 30.82 per dollar, its strongest since July 2000, before ending\par the day at 30.86. Foreigners pumped a net T$136 billion into\par local stocks since the start of February but turned net sellers\par for the second time in a month on Thursday.\par     The Thai baht fell a third of a percent on concern the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's decision on Wednesday to raise interest rates to\par ward off inflation could slow growth and discourage foreign\par investors who have driven a four-month stock rally.\par     In Taiwan, the equity inflows since February helped the\par Taiwan dollar overcome \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the past\par week aimed at stalling the gains.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The inflows also helped the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  emerge as the top performer in Asia this year.\par  \par     "It's got a lot to do with the turnaround in the technology\par sector," said Song Seng Wun, economist at GK Goh Securities.\par     "Also, if you don't have any quarrels with the mainland\par then it helps," he said, referring to improving ties since\par China allowed direct flights from Taiwan in February.\par     Signs of a revival in domestic consumer demand helped push\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 up the South Korean won to about 1,006 per dollar. The gains  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 were capped by concerns about won-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Korea.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves climbed 1.2 percent  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in February to a record $202.16 billion. The pace of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 accumulation quickened from January after authorities appeared  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to step up their dollar buying to keep the won competitive  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against rivals.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The won has surged almost 10 percent against the yen since  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the end of October. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has lost ground since it hit a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 seven-year high of 998.1 per dollar last week.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BAHT STUMBLES  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Thai baht, which has gained nearly 7 percent in the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 past four months, lost ground after the benchmark stock index  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 hit a one-month low because of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate rise and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 oil prices touching a four-month high.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Foreign equity inflows have been phenomenal in the past  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 four months," said Danny Suwanapruti, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 4CAST Ltd. in Singapore. "The baht could be hurt if there is a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 sharp reversal in the inflows."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Song said some investors saw the Bank of Thailand's move as  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 too hasty, especially as the economy faces a slowdown this  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 year.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "People were wondering whether the BOT is overly aggressive\par and undermining economic growth," he said.\par     The Indonesian rupiah weakened on a seasonal surge in\par demand for dollars by local companies.\par     Song said he still forecasts a 9 percent appreciation in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the rupiah by the end of the year to 8,500 per dollar as  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono implements plans to bring  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 back foreign direct investments and push up the pace of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economic growth. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0800 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.10         104.63       -0.45\par  Sing dlr        1.6280         1.6257       -0.14\par  Taiwan dlr      30.855         30.878       +0.07\par  Korean won     1006.10        1007.20       +0.11\par  Baht             38.41          38.33       -0.21\par  Peso             54.93          54.79       -0.25\par  Rupiah         9282.00        9265.00       -0.18\par  Rupee            43.66          43.69       +0.07\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       105.10         102.45       -2.52\par  Sing dlr        1.6280         1.6310       +0.18\par  Taiwan dlr      30.855         31.920       +3.45\par  Korean won     1006.10        1035.10       +2.88\par  Baht             38.41          38.88       +1.22\par  Peso             54.93          56.28       +2.47\par  Rupiah         9282.00        9290.00       +0.09\par  Rupee            43.66          43.47       -0.44 ((Editing by\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 John Mair; rajat.bhattacharya@reuters.com; Reuters Messaging:  \f28 \p