\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  reserves up amid signs of  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 22:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SEOUL, March 3 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reserves rose in February, data showed on Thursday, with the\par growth pace quickening from January after authorities appeared to\par step up \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the won hit seven-year\par highs.\par     South Korean reserves, the world's fourth-largest, climbed\par 1.2 percent to a new record of $202.16 billion by end-February\par from $199.7 billion at the end of January, the Bank of Korea said\par in a statement.\par     The increase was still below the 3.4 percent rise in December\par and 8 percent gain in November, but marked an acceleration from a\par 0.3 percent advance in January as dealers suggested authorities\par had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after the won hit a seven-year high of 998.1 per\par dollar last week.\par     The won's surge against the dollar was partly due to a\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  report on reserves that had knocked the U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In a report outlining its 2005 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to parliament, the\par Bank of Korea said it would diversify its reserves away from\par government bonds into high yielding paper and other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stressed later the plan didn't mean it would\par convert dollars into other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  but it could put future\par inflows into a more diverse set of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and instruments\par than the U.S. dollar and U.S. Treasuries.\par     The won                  , which was Asia's best performing\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 2004 with a 15 percent rise to the U.S. dollar, is up\par 2.8 percent so far this year.\par     Dealers have suggested South Korea, which has Asia's\par third-largest economy, might be relaxing its policy to tolerate a\par slight rise in the won to help dampen any inflationary pressures\par as authorities attempt to kick-start depressed local demand.\par     But analysts say South Korea has not abandoned a long-held\par policy of curbing the won in a bid to keep its exports\par competitive, especially since exports have been the main driver\par of economic growth over the past two years.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  attributed the rise in reserves to interest\par payments on its investment into U.S. Treasuries and a rise in the\par value of euro denominated assets when converted into dollars.\par  \par     South Korean foreign reserves ($ billion):\par     End-Feb   End-Jan   End-Dec   End-Nov   End-Oct   End-Sept\par     202.162   199.699   199.066   192.602   178.388   174.448.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050302e13200gfz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
