\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Down as China, G7 expectations pared.  \b0\par\par\uc2 877 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2005\par 09:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 31 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were pushed\par lower on Monday as markets scaled back their expectations for\par an imminent Chinese yuan revaluation and for the upcoming Group\par of Seven nations' meeting to put more pressure on the region.\par     That happened after fresh comments from Chinese top\par officials suggested they were in no hurry to reform the yuan\par regime, and the U.S. dollar found support ahead of key data and\par a Federal Reserve  policy meeting.\par     Traders braced for a volatile week that will end with the\par Group of Seven nations' meeting in London on Friday and\par Saturday and could see U.S. rates raised by another 25 basis\par points.\par     U.S. Treasury Undersecretary John Taylor added to the\par pressure on regionals with his remarks that there was no need\par for the dollar to crash and that the G7 statement would not be\par different from the one issued last year in Florida.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Officials\par from China, India and other emerging economies have been\par invited to talks with the seven industrialised nations.\par  \par     The Korean won fell from near Friday's 7-year high of 1,023\par a dollar to around 1,026.\par     The Singapore dollar fell about a quarter percent to 1.64 a\par dollar and then trimmed losses. The Thai baht and Indonesian\par rupiah were down.\par     There was talk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Singapore and in the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippines, where the peso barely moved after its rapid 2.3  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent gains in 3 weeks, helped by a 12 percent rally in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 stocks  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bhanu Baweja, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with UBS, said even if  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the G7 called on Asia to share in the adjustment of the massive  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. trade deficit by letting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rise, the region would  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 not oblige readily.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Even if the rhetoric is stepped up on level to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 burden-sharing, I believe it will not be very significant for  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "What is central for Asian authorities is that economic  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 growth in most areas is clearly off the peak. They will  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 continue to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to protect against sharp appreciation in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , thereby trying to keep exports competitive,"  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines released data on Monday showing annual  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 gross domestic product grew 6.1 percent in 2004, the quickest  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 pace in 15 years. But growth in the last quarter of 2004 was  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 disappointing, and analysts warned the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market was  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 probably overestimating potential investment inflows and  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 remittances.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DOLLAR SUPPORTED  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, the see-sawing on the prospects of China  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 revaluing its virtually pegged yuan continued, with China's  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 deputy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Li Ruogu dashing expectations by  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 saying China did not have the capacity to address global  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economic imbalances and was not willing or able to do it.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The premium on one-year yuan in non-deliverable forwards  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 was down to 3,850 points, pricing in 4.9 percent gains,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 compared with 5.6 percent on Friday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Global oil prices fell, with U.S. oil below $47 a barrel,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 after OPEC producers left output unchanged and Iraq's election  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 passed without disruption to oil exports.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "The dollar will bounce this week," said Claudio Piron,\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with JP Morgan.\par     "Oil prices are lower and that should help the dollar. The\par Fed FOMC will be delivering 25 basis points and positioning in\par Asia is very aggressive," he said.\par     YEN-WON CROSS\par     Piron said the north Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would suffer, but\par that markets would be divided on whether to buy the won against\par the yen. The yen-won cross rate showed the yen at 9.89 won.\par     Markets have been torn between the urge to buy the yen-won\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 cross below the 10 mark - which they believe is the highest  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 level for the won Korean authorities can tolerate - and the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 belief that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily, since the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 government is running out of bonds to offset the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders waited for data on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves from  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea for evidence of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in January and confirmation  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of their view that Korea \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  less in order to stabilise  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 its bond markets.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The finance ministry's announcement on Friday that it would  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 issue 5 trillion won in fiscal bonds in February, however,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 frustrated some won bulls. That came after Korea said it would  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 cut down on the amount of treasuries issued in February.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0803 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.53         103.16       -0.36\par  Sing dlr        1.6362         1.6358       -0.02\par  Taiwan dlr      31.790         31.802       +0.04\par  Korean won     1025.50        1023.50       -0.20\par  Baht             38.53          38.45       -0.21\par  Peso             55.09          55.09       +0.00\par  Rupiah         9160.00        9144.00       -0.17\par  Rupee            43.71          43.72       +0.02\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.53         102.45       -1.04\par  Sing dlr        1.6362         1.6310       -0.32\par  Taiwan dlr      31.790         31.917       +0.40\par  Korean won     1025.50        1035.10       +0.94\par  Baht             38.53          38.85       +0.83\par  Peso             55.09          56.28       +2.16\par  Rupiah         9160.00        9270.00       +1.20\p