\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea bonds close sharply lower on supply woes.   \b0\par\par\uc2 561 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2005\par 09:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     SEOUL, Jan 31 (Reuters) - South Korean government bond prices\par plunged on Monday, hit by concerns about an increase in debt\par supplies from the finance ministry and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Sentiment was hit hard after the finance ministry said last\par week it would issue a total of 5 trillion won ($4.88 billion) in\par fiscal bonds in February, after scaling back the size of next\par month's treasury bond issuance.\par     Investors were reluctant to send out buy orders amid fears\par the finance ministry may also move to issue more treasuries to\par fund \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to rein in a\par surging won \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has to refinance some 12 trillion won worth\par of maturing monetary stabilisation bonds in February, which made\par investors more anxious about purchasing bonds.\par     "The market is spooked by concerns about overall supply\par conditions, holding investors back from trading," said an analyst\par at a local investment trust company.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "But I think the yield has reached the level of overshooting\par and could stabilise ahead of the Lunar New Year holidays," he\par added.\par     The yield on three-year treasury bonds\par jumped 12 basis points to close at 4.06 percent, its highest\par since Aug. 9 last year when it hit 4.08 percent.\par     The rise follows an 11-basis-point jump on Friday.\par     The five-year treasury bond yield            also surged 10\par basis points to end at 4.32 percent.\par  \par                                           close   prev close\par  10-yr treasury bonds                  4.85 pct     4.75 pct\par  5-yr treasury bonds                   4.32 pct     4.22 pct\par  3-yr treasury bonds                   4.06 pct     3.94 pct\par  3-yr corporate bonds                  4.53 pct     4.42 pct\par  2-yr monetary stabilisation bonds     4.05 pct     3.94 pct\par  1-yr treasury bonds                   3.76 pct     3.64 pct\par  1-yr monetary stabilisation bonds     3.75 pct     3.69 pct\par  3-mth CDs                             3.57 pct     3.59 pct\par  Average interbank call                3.35 pct            ~\par  Average call rate                     3.22 pct            ~\par  ~ Not available\par  * Quoted by the Korea Securities Dealers Association\par  -----------------------------------------------------------\par     South Korea's won closed slightly lower on Monday but was\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 still within sight of seven-year highs versus the dollar hit on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Friday, fanning concerns the government may issue bonds to fund   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is known to favour a cheaper won to maintain the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 price competitiveness of exports, the sole driver of economic   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 growth during an extended slump in domestic consumption.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, a senior official at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  told Reuters   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Korea would consider how bearish sentiment was in the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 local debt market before deciding the amount of monetary   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 stabilisation bonds (MSBs) to be issued for this week.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After the market closed, the bank said it would sell a total   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of 4 trillion won in MSBs on Tuesday. It said it would hold an   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 auction to sell 1 trillion won in 364-day MSBs on Friday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On the supply front, the finance ministry said on Monday it   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 auctioned 1.37 trillion won in three-year treasury bonds at 4.10   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent, with bids totalling 2 trillion won.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     On the Korea Futures Exchange, the key March contract for\par three-year treasuries  fell 24 ticks to 110.65.\par     The benchmark Korea Composite Stock Price Index         ended\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 up 1.21 percent.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ($1=1024.0 Won).   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050131e11v0096s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
