\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea bonds drop early, supply worries weigh.   \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Januar 2005\par 02:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Jan 31 (Reuters) - South Korean government bond prices slid by mid-morning on Monday, hit by the prospects of massive fiscal bond supplies amid worries about a potential rise in treasury bond offerings for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By 0114 GMT, the yield on three-year treasury bonds             was\par offered up 11 basis points to 4.05 percent, while the five-year\par treasury bond yield            was bid 13 basis points higher at 4.35\par percent, dealers said.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2  "Bond market sentiment was hurt due to concerns about fiscal bond issuance amid growing worries the finance ministry may increase debt offerings to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," said Rhee Seung-hee, an economist at Hyundai Investment Trust Management.    \par \par \uc2  "But given that economic fundamentals are showing no improvement, we expect bond yields to stabilise soon."    \par \par \uc2  The finance ministry said on Friday it would issue a total of 5 trillion won ($4.88 billion) in 91-day fiscal bonds after it had scaled back the treasury bond offering for February.    \par \par \uc2  South Korea's won hit seven-year highs on Friday, fanning concerns the government may issue bonds to fund its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  is known to favour a cheaper won to maintain the price competitiveness of exports, the sole driver of economic growth during an extended slump in domestic consumption.    \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, a senior official at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  told Reuters the Bank of Korea would consider how bearish sentiment was in the local debt market before deciding the amount of monetary stabilisation bonds (MSBs) to be issued for this week.    \par \par \uc2  The official, who declined to be named, said by telephone he expected the market would stabilise after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced its weekly auction plan at 4 p.m. (0700 GMT).    \par \par \uc2  On the supply front, the finance ministry is due to auction 1.37 trillion won in three-year treasury bonds in the morning session.    \par \par \uc2  On the Korea Futures Exchange, the key March contract for three-year treasuries  fell 28 ticks to 110.61.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050131e11v001us\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
