\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Taiwan dlr leads decline - baht gains.  \b0\par\par\uc2 667 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 2005\par 09:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 18 (Reuters) - The Taiwan dollar led Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lower on Tuesday on worries that U.S. capital\par inflows data and a string of scheduled speeches by U.S. Fed\par officials could ease market concerns about the U.S. dollar's\par prospects.\par     The Taiwan dollar lost a quarter of a percent and the\par Singapore dollar, Indian rupee and the rupiah each lost around\par a fifth of a percent, following the lead of the yen, which\par weakened almost a percent from Monday's five-year high against\par the dollar.\par     U.S. capital inflow figures for November are due at 1400\par GMT on Tuesday. A reading close to the record U.S. trade\par deficit of $60.3 billion for November would alleviate some\par worries that the United States is unable to plug its record\par current account deficit.\par     "Stronger-than-expected net inflows may lend the dollar a\par bit of support against the Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said David\par Simmonds, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Royal Bank of Scotland in\par Singapore.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Traders will monitor comments from four U.S. Federal\par Reserve officials, due to speak on Tuesday, for signals that\par U.S. interest rates might rise faster than expected.\par     Royal Bank of Scotland expects the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par raise its benchmark rate by 25 basis points at each of its\par eight meetings this year, a pace that is faster than the\par markets' current expectations.\par     "The Fed is sounding hawkish," said Simmonds. "Asia would\par be the most vulnerable if there are signs that the Fed is\par behind the inflation curve and starts tightening much harder.\par We're not there yet."\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FEAR\par     Fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also hurt Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday\par after several had reached multi-year highs on Monday. South\par Korea's won traded at a seven-year high on Monday.\par     Analysts say central banks in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Taiwan,\par Singapore and India have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  repeatedly in the past\par year, curbing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength to keep their exports\par competitive. Bank of Japan has stayed away from such\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since March 2004.\par     "We think that the risks of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over the next few\par weeks are very high and should the Bank of Japan finally\par re-emerge in the markets, it will likely be with a bang,"\par Ashley Davies, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at UBS in Singapore, said\par in a report.\par  \par     UBS expects the yen to weaken to 103 per dollar in the next\par one to three months.\par     The Thai baht bucked the weaker trend by gaining a tenth of\par a percent to levels just short of the 4-=   year high reached\par on Monday.\par     Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said on\par Monday he wasn't concerned by the baht's strength.\par     Claudio Piron, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at JP Morgan, expects\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the baht, and the Taiwan dollar, to outperform against the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Singapore dollar and other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year on the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par back of growing foreign investments into Thai stocks and a rise\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in domestic investments.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Earnings reports due from the banking sector by January 21\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par should also support the outlook for increasing credit demand\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on day at 0800 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       102.63         102.07       -0.55\par  Sing dlr        1.6367         1.6330       -0.23\par  Taiwan dlr      31.893         31.804       -0.28\par  Korean won     1035.70        1035.70       +0.00\par  Baht             38.47          38.50       +0.08\par  Peso             55.65          55.53       -0.22\par  Rupiah         9150.00        9133.00       -0.19\par  Rupee            43.76          43.66       -0.23\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       102.63         102.45       -0.18\par  Sing dlr        1.6367         1.6310       -0.35\par  Taiwan dlr      31.893         31.920       +0.08\par  Korean won     1035.70        1035.10       -0.06\par  Baht             38.47          38.88       +1.07\par  Peso             55.65          56.28       +1.14\par  Rupiah         9150.00        9290.00       +1.53\par  Rupee            43.76          43.47       -0.66.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050118e11i008ya\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
