\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won ends lower,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears weigh.  \b0\par\par\uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2005\par 08:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     SEOUL, Jan 4 (Reuters) - The South Korean won ended a shade\par lower on Tuesday, weighed down by fears about possible government\par dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but losses were capped as many\par players saw the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakness extending into 2005.\par  \par     The won                   settled in domestic trade at\par 1,038.7 per dollar, compared with Monday's close of 1,038.1.\par     Warnings by a finance ministry official that the government\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 would increase, if necessary, the ceiling on bond issuances to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 fund \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had little impact,  \par \par \uc2 dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "The cautious mood dominated the market," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 trader. "Investors are holding onto the view that the dollar's  \par \par \uc2 weakness will continue but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fears halted any brave  \par \par \uc2 attempts to place sizable won-buying orders."  \par \par \uc2 Choi Joong-kyung, head of the finance ministry's  \par \par \uc2 international finance bureau, told Reuters in an interview that  \par \par \uc2 the won's recent gains against the dollar appeared excessive  \par \par \uc2 given a sluggish domestic economy.  \par \par \uc2 "The won's recent rises have been rather excessive even if we  \par \par \uc2 take into account the global trend of a softer dollar that became  \par \par \uc2 more pronounced since last October," Choi said.  \par \par \uc2 "If there is a justification, the government will push ahead  \par \par \uc2 to increase the ceiling on treasury bond issues to finance  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added.  \par \par \uc2 The government plans to sell 5 trillion won in treasury bonds  \par \par \uc2 for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January alone, a record  \par \par \uc2 monthly issuance for such a purpose.  \par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data released on Tuesday showed the country's  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rose 3.4 percent in December to a  \par \par \uc2 record high as dealers pointed to further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by  \par \par \uc2 authorities to control the won's strength.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's reserves rose to $199.07 billion at the end of\par December from $192.60 billion a month before.\par     The yen       , which the won usually follows closely, last\par quoted at 102.56/60 per dollar, up slightly from 102.71 late in\par New York on Monday.\par     The dollar rebounded on Monday after last week's heavy\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 sell-off but analysts were uncertain if the rally would hold up  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 after fresh economic data suggested the December U.S. jobs report  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 due on Friday might not live up to market expectations.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The local stock market         ended down 0.76 percent with\par foreign investors buying net 40.6 billion won worth.\par                        0700 GMT         0030 GMT      prev close\par  Won                    1,038.7          1,039.8         1,038.1\par  *Yen/won            10.1090/49       10.1079/58      10.1002/51\par  ~NDF 1-mth won    1,039.2/40.2      1,040.0/1.0     1,038.9/9.9\par  ~NDF 3-mth won    1,039.6/40.6      1,041.1/2.1    1,039.2/40.2\par  Stocks KOSPI            886.90           891.99          893.71\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * calculated based on each \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rates against the dollar  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ~ non-deliverable forward rates quoted by Prebon Yamane Asia  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pacific.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050104e1140086l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
