\par\par \b \uc2 South Korea's  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  policy - running against the global tide?  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Yoo Choonsik  \par \uc2 796 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 2004\par 06:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Dec 17 (Reuters) - South Korea is ready to spend trillions more won next year to control its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and try to keep its stuttering economy growing, a policy analysts say is an expensive failure that has cost $15 billion this year.   \par \par \uc2  The won has risen 12.6 percent against the dollar so far in 2004, hitting a 7-year high this month, despite official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  based on fears a surging won would derail exports.   \par \par \uc2  The finance ministry is positioning for another big year of buying dollars in 2005, yet analysts say South Korea cannot stand in the way of a widespread decline in the U.S. dollar caused by Washington's large budget and current account deficits.   \par \par \uc2  "The effect on exports from the won's value is getting increasingly limited now, and the dollar's weakness is now taking place globally and on a wider scope than before," said Lim Ji-won, an economist at JP Morgan Chase.   \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  released figures showing \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves had risen $3.4 billion in the first half of December, citing "smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 " in the won as a factor.   \par \par \uc2  Reserves now stand at at a record $196 billion, the fourth largest in the world, having almost doubled in three years.   \par \par \uc2  The finance ministry could claim success in 2003, when heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped the won stay flat against the dollar, the main \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for South Korean exports.   \par \par \uc2  In contrast, Japan - a trade competitor and another to heavily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to manage its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - saw its yen gain 11 percent in 2003.   \par \par \uc2  But in 2004 the competitive edge has been eroded. The yen has risen just 2.7 percent, taking the relative values of the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to where they were two years ago at just over 10 won per yen.   \par \par \uc2  $300 A HEAD   \par \par \uc2  Opposition politicians say the ministry - which wants to raise treasury bonds worth 21.9 trillion won ($20.6 billion) next year to fund \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  - has merely delayed the won's rise through a policy that some analysts estimate has cost more than $300 per person in \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year alone.   \par \par \uc2  "Its massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has proved a failure as we now see the fast appreciation to a level before the massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  began," said Oh Suk-tae, an economist at Citigroup. "The effect of its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will from now be very limited."   \par \par \uc2  The finance ministry is determined to foster exports as they are the main driver of growth in South Korea, with consumers still loath to open their wallets after a credit bubble burst two years ago.   \par \par \uc2  There are also fears that the attempt to limit the won's rise has fuelled inflation, by exposing South Korea to high energy and commodity prices. Inflation hit 3.8 percent in the year through October, although the rate eased back to 3.3 percent in November.   \par \par \uc2  While the government can print won as it likes, Oh estimates it has cost the government at least $15 billion to carry its huge \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which are mostly in dollars.   \par \par \uc2  Analysts say a weaker won may have helped exporters win orders when the global economy was buoyant but demand for South Korea's high-tech goods has cooled and the impact has waned.   \par \par \uc2  UNDETERRED   \par \par \uc2  Government officials are also debating whether they can really keep a cap on the won. Facing criticism from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , finance ministry official Choi Joong-kyung broke months of silence this week to argue \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy was an important tool to support exports.   \par \par \uc2  "The exchange rate is and will continue to be an important macroeconomic policy tool," Choi, the head of the ministry's international bureau and an influential \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy maker, told reporters.   \par \par \uc2  It was a direct challenge to an assistant governor at the Bank of Korea, Rhee Yeung-kyun, who told a seminar on Monday \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates should not be a policy tool to support local firms and the government could not be expected to keep the exchange rates at a certain level.   \par \par \uc2  Next year's limit on bond issuance for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  is 16 percent higher than the 18.8 trillion issued this year. Dealers said some of the extra will be used to square \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions taken this year.   \par \par \uc2  They wonder when the finance ministry will tire of its dollar buying and realise it can not hold back the tide.   \par \par \uc2  "The dollar's drop is a global pattern now and the ministry won't try to run counter the trend," said Chung In-woo, executive \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi's Seoul branch. data. (US$1=1,061 won) (Additional reporting by Cheon Jong-woo).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041217e0ch00692\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
