\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Retreat alongside yen as US dlr rebounds.  \b0\par\par\uc2 722 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2004\par 04:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 9 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  retreated\par further from recent multi-year highs on Thursday, following the\par Japanese yen, as the U.S. dollar extended a corrective rebound\par against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The dollar's recovery this week, which some see as a pause\par in a longer-term decline, has been helped by several factors,\par including increased verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the Japanese and\par European authorities.\par     A decision by high-yielders, Australia and Canada, to hold\par interest rates steady and the weight of positions stacked\par against the dollar in recent months also led to the dollar\par buying.\par     Within Asia, the Korean won, which had outperformed in the\par rally, has suffered the biggest losses this week, shedding\par nearly 2 percent from seven-year highs. It was quoted around\par 1,057 a dollar, some 20 won off that peak.\par     The Singapore dollar, Indian rupee and the Taiwan dollar\par have also dropped a percent each this week.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  The yen has fallen\par over two percent from 5-year highs.\par     The worries of a sovereign ratings downgrade dragged down\par the Philippine peso and rupiah selling by oil importers kept\par the Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around 9,180 a dollar, near two-month\par lows.\par     Jimmy Koh, head of research at United Overseas Bank in\par Singapore, said expectations that China will revalue its yuan\par sometime next year underpinned the regionals, based on the view\par that a firmer yuan will make Asian authorities more tolerant of\par gains.\par     Chinese yuan non-deliverable forwards showed markets have\par pared expectations of a near-term change in the tightly managed\par yuan, after China's key annual economic policy meeting at the\par weekend failed to provide clues on yuan policy.\par  \par     But one-year NDFs still priced in an appreciation of over\par five percent from current levels around 8.278 yuan per dollar.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FEARS HAUNT\par     Markets fear Asian central banks will use the momentum of\par the dollar rebound to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and push their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  down\par faster.\par     Data from an auction of U.S. Treasuries on Wednesday showed\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 65 percent of the total $15 billion sale was picked up by\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par indirect bidders, including foreign central banks, adding to\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par evidence from recent reserves data that showed Asian central\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily in November.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reserves data showed more than $10 billion of the $14\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion increase in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's November reserves could have\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resulted from dollar-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the won's\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strength.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bhanu Baweja, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist with UBS, said in a note\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that this was Korea's largest monthly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on record,\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and the won's appreciation of more than 6 percent in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade-weighted terms last month was also the strongest gain on\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par record.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said around $3 billion of a $4.3 billion increase\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in Singapore's November reserves could not be explained by\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par simple valuation effects, and was possibly due to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The reserves totalled $110.1 billion.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korea left interest rates unchanged at a policy meeting on\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday. Economists had been divided on the chances of another\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cut in rates, already at a record low, with some speculating\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that the won's rise gave the Bank of Korea room to ease policy\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par further.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The BoK, working for the MoF (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ),\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par certainly seems to have the stomach for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Baweja\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Note that the opportunity cost for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is actually\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par falling as the credit cycle gets weaker and interest rates fall\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in Korea," he said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  Change on the day at   0252 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.17         103.70       -0.45\par  Sing dlr        1.6448         1.6465       +0.10\par  Taiwan dlr      32.306         32.260       -0.14\par  Korean won     1055.60        1058.50       +0.27\par  Baht             39.39          39.34       -0.13\par  Peso             56.13          56.08       -0.09\par  Rupiah         9193.00        9182.00       -0.12\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.17         107.31       +3.01\par  Sing dlr        1.6448         1.6978       +3.22\par  Taiwan dlr      32.306         33.978       +5.18\par  Korean won     1055.60        1192.00      +12.92\par  Baht             39.39          39.59       +0.50\par  Peso             56.13          55.49       -1.14\par  Rupiah         9193.00        8410.00       -8.52\par  Rupee            44.02          45.60       +3.58.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041209e0c90038p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
