\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Baht, Sing dollar lead decline.  \b0\par\par\uc2 769 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2004\par 10:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 3 (Reuters) - The Thai baht lost almost 1\par percent on Friday as Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  declined on growing\par expectations that central banks would sell their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par stem a rally that could hurt the region's exporters.\par     The baht        weakened from a seven-month high against\par the dollar to about 39.48 per dollar. The Singapore dollar\par  , the Taiwan dollar  and the Indonesian rupiah\par   lost more than half a percent each, following a 1.5\par percent drop in the yen.\par     Central bankers and government officials in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par and\par  Japan have issued repeated warnings they may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem\par a two-month rally in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  which they say have\par become overvalued compared with economic fundamentals.\par     "Central banks across Asia will be wary of speculative\par attacks on their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Lian Chia Chiang, an\par economist at JP Morgan Chase in Singapore.\par     Still, Lian does not expect the dollar's weakening trend to\par reverse anytime soon.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  JP Morgan expects the baht to appreciate\par to 39 per dollar by the end of the year and to 37 per dollar by\par September next year.\par     The baht has underperformed most other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par this year, partly on concerns about violence in its southern\par region. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has gained 0.4 percent this year, compared\par with a 14 percent surge in the South Korean won\par   and a near 4 percent gain in the yen.\par  \par     Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devaluka said on\par Friday the baht was still competitive for exports.\par     Lian said the strength of Thailand's economy -- which he\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 expects to grow 5 percent in 2005 compared with 6 percent  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 growth this year - and a broadly weakening dollar will help  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 boost the baht's value next year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. DOLLAR RESILIENCE  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The north Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the Singapore dollar took a  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 beating after South Korean President Roh Moo-hyun said in  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 London on Thursday that the government was ready to guard  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 against excessive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves and aims to coordinate such  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 measures with other governments.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Data released Thursday showed the South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in November, although the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan has stayed away from the markets since March.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Song Seng Wun, economist at Singapore-based G.K. Goh  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Securities said both central banks may use thin trading in the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 upcoming Christmas and year-end holiday season to sell their  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and reverse the two-month rally that took the won to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a seven-year high and the yen to a five-year high this week.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar could also get support from the recovery in the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. economy which has forced the U.S. Federal Reserve to raise  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 benchmark rates this year. Most analysts expect the Fed to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 raise rates once more at a meeting this month.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some traders who sold the dollar this month on concerns  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 about the widening U.S. current account and budget deficits  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 reversed their bets ahead of the release of U.S. non-farm  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 payrolls data later on Friday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. economy created 180,000 non-farm jobs in November,  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 after 337,000 jobs created in October, according to the median  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of a Reuters poll of economists. "There's a bit more  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 resilience to the U.S. economy than many people think," said  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Song.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Song said expectations for stronger U.S. data and fears of  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would stall the dollar's slide  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in the shorter term, although the longer-term forecast was for  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a further decline in the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day at 0824 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.36         101.98       -1.34\par  Sing dlr        1.6426         1.6317       -0.66\par  Taiwan dlr      32.191         31.990       -0.62\par  Korean won     1045.30        1041.40       -0.37\par  Baht             39.42          39.11       -0.79\par  Rupiah         9060.00        9015.00       -0.50\par  Rupee            44.17          44.04       -0.31\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.36         107.31       +3.82\par  Sing dlr        1.6426         1.6978       +3.36\par  Taiwan dlr      32.191         33.978       +5.55\par  Korean won     1045.30        1192.00      +14.03\par  Baht             39.42          39.59       +0.42\par  Rupiah         9060.00        8410.00       -7.17\par  Rupee            44.17          45.60       +3.23 ((Editing by\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Neil Fullick; rajat.bhattacharya@reuters.com; Reuters  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Messaging: rajat.bhattacharya.reuters.com@reuters.net; +65 6870  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 3841))  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For the new Reuters scrolling global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  service please  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 click .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041203e0c30083y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
