\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Weaken on data,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears.  \b0\par\par\uc2 631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2004\par 04:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Rajat Bhattacharya\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 30 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened on\par Tuesday after disappointing economic data from Japan and\par comments from Asian leaders calling for concerted action to\par stall a two-month rally in their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The Taiwan dollar          lost about 0.4 percent in early\par deals to 32.28 per dollar. The South Korean won\par   shed 0.1 percent to about 1,048 per dollar.\par     Last week, the Taiwan dollar had climbed to its strongest\par level in four years while the won had appreciated to a\par seven-year high.\par     The rally stalled on Monday due to worries about likely\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  across Asia. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 South Korea\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par presidential office said on Monday that the leaders of Japan,\par China and South Korea agreed on the sidelines of the\par Association of South-East Asian Nations (ASEAN) summit in Laos\par on the need for stable exchange rates.\par     Meanwhile, industrial production data from South Korea and\par Japan disappointed markets.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japanese data showed industrial\par output unexpectedly fell 1.6 percent in October from a month\par earlier. On Monday, South Korea said industrial output fell 0.9\par percent in October.\par     "The weak Japanese and Korean data are making people\par conclude that the U.S. economy is cyclically the strongest\par now," said Simon Flint, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Bank of\par America in Singapore.\par     Some traders and investors, who had bid up the won and\par other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this month on concerns about prolonged\par weakness in the dollar, probably rewound their bets after the\par agreement among Asian leaders that the rally in their\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was overdone, Flint said.\par     "The talk about that meeting may have had an impact on the\par market," he said. "The decline in the dollar has been arrested\par for the time being."\par     Further data from Japan, including gross domestic product\par figures and the Tankan survey due early next month, is likely\par to reconfirm that the Japanese economy may be slowing.\par     Bank of America still expects the dollar to weaken to 100\par yen by the end of the year, from around 103.15 on Tuesday, and\par to $1.35 per euro, from $1.325 on Tuesday, because of the\par widening U.S. current account deficits.\par     Traders are looking for further clues on whether Asian\par central banks are curtailing purchases of U.S. treasury bills\par and other dollar assets in their foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserve\par holdings.\par     A Chinese economic adviser said last week U.S. government\par data showed that China, which holds the world's second-largest\par foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves, reduced its dollar holdings.\par     Many other Asian central banks could reduce their dollar\par holdings if the dollar weakness persists and that could lead to\par further dollar weakness in the longer term, Flint said.\par     "I don't think this question is going to go away soon,"\par Flint said. "There's enough structural themes pointing to a\par dollar weakness in the longer term." \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par  \par Change on the day at   0313 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.22         103.07       -0.15\par  Sing dlr        1.6412         1.6410       -0.01\par  Taiwan dlr      32.172         32.155       -0.05\par  Korean won     1047.90        1046.90       -0.10\par  Baht             39.57          39.52       -0.13\par  Peso             56.17          56.13       -0.07\par  Rupiah         9022.00        9010.00       -0.13 Change on\par year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       103.22         107.31       +3.96\par  Sing dlr        1.6412         1.6978       +3.45\par  Taiwan dlr      32.172         33.978       +5.61\par  Korean won     1047.90        1192.00      +13.75\par  Baht             39.57          39.59       +0.04\par  Peso             56.17          55.49       -1.20\par  Rupiah         9022.00        8410.00       -6.78\par  Rupee            44.79          45.60       +1.80.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041130e0bu0038p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
