\par\par \b \uc2 S.Korea won ends off 7-yr high,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  cited.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Yoo Choonsik  \par \uc2 640 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2004\par 09:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  SEOUL, Nov 22 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 South Korea\b0 \highlight\uc2 's won  closed local trade higher against the dollar on Monday, but pared its gains on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after hitting a fresh seven-year high earlier during the session, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2  The won  closed local trade up 0.3 percent on the day at 1,065.3 per dollar, after paring some of its early gains on what dealers said was selling on behalf of the authorities.   \par \par \uc2  The selling, which briefly pushed the won below Friday's local close of 1,068.7 in the afternoon, followed a rare request by the finance minister for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  more strongly in the market.   \par \par \uc2  Dealers said a flood of dollars were still awaiting to hit the market and the impact of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was only likely to slow the won's rise as long as the dollar's global weakness persists.   \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not very strong today. The dollar/won won't turn up unless the dollar/yen rose to somewhere above 105," said Jung In-woo, executive \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi's Seoul branch.   \par \par \uc2  The yen  stood at 103.27/30 per dollar at 0733 GMT, down slightly on the day but still in sight of the 102.70 hit in New York on Friday, the highest level since March 2000. The yen is closely watched by dealers in Seoul, given the strong competition between the two neighbours in export markets.   \par \par \uc2  "Exporters appeared hasty to sell dollars while importers preferred to wait a little more," Jung said, indicating that exporters still had a lot of dollars to sell.   \par \par \uc2  EXPORTS ALREADY SLOWING   \par \par \uc2  The strength of the won, which has gained 6 percent this month against the dollar and 12 percent so far this year, also sent the local stock market  tumbling about 2 percent.   \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Monday, Finance Minister Lee Hun-jai asked the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief, Park Seung, to take a stronger stance to cap the won's rise, according to a government source.   \par \par \uc2  "He asked Governor Park that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  take bolder and more aggressive counter measures," the source said by telephone, adding that this could include the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  using its right to print money.   \par \par \uc2  In non-deliverable forward trading, the one-month won was quoted at 1,066.0/7.0 late on Monday, against 1,069.5/70.5 late on Friday, according to Prebon Yamane Asia Pacific. Three-month won rose to 1,067.4/8.4, from 1,070.9/1.9.   \par \par \uc2  The rare meeting between Lee and the governor of the Bank of Korea came as the won's rally raised concerns about the export-dependent economy being damaged as slowing exports combine with a persistent slump in local demand.   \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Korea has taken the leading role in controlling the won's rise since the finance ministry was criticised last month in parliament for keeping the won undervalued.   \par \par \uc2  The amount of money the ministry can mobilise to fund \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also been limited by parliament.   \par \par \uc2  The rising won has added to concerns about Chinese demand for exports after Beijing raised interest rates for the first time in nine years to step up a drive to cool its economy.   \par \par \uc2  China is the largest market for South Korean exports, soaking up a fifth of its total shipments abroad.   \par \par \uc2  Last week the finance minister all but abandoned a long-standing target of 5 percent economic growth this year, saying the chance of meeting the forecast was extremely slim.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The firmer won also hit export-reliant manufacturers on the Seoul stock\par market. Chipmaker Samsung Electronics Co. Ltd.  fell 3.1 percent and\par automaker Hyundai Motor Co.             lost 2.4 percent. (Additional\par reporting by Lee Shin-hyung and Cheon Jong-woo).\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041122e0bm0063o\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (South Korea near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \l